const KB_SEED = [{"category": "SLAs & Urgent Cases","title": "SLAs","content": "**Chargeback / Manual release SLA**\n\n### **⏱️ 3 Business Days**\n- BDC Deposit (Failed / Reversal)\n- BDC Withdrawal\n- Fawry Deposit\n\n### **⏱️ 5 Business Days**\n- Non-BDC Withdrawal\n- Non-BDC Withdrawal via Apple Pay (below 350 EGP)\n- Fawry Withdrawal (Cairoxx)\n- Manual release: Validate the receipt within **1 Business Day** and **5 Business Days** from the transaction date (Trx status -> Authorized)\n\n### **⏱️ 10 Business Days**\n- BDC Withdrawal via Apple Pay\n\n### **⏱️ Up to 45 Days**\n- Mastercard Chargebacks (Online / POS)\n- Non-BDC Withdrawal via Apple Pay (above 350 EGP)\n\n### **❗ No SLA**\n- Non-BDC Deposit\n\n**SLAs**\n### **⏱️ Instant**\n● **Dashboard**\n- Reactivate the deleted account\n- Unlock account (Not sealed lock)\n- Log out of the device\n- Mark as ready for activation\n- Cancel standard re-order card\n● **Jira**\n- Urgent call (30 Minutes)\n- Waffarha Voucher - Urgent (1 Hour)\n● **Slack**\n- Reject Card design (ID channel and 2 H during business days)\n\n### **⏱️ 1 Business Day**\n● **Dashboard**\n- Update mobile Number at MDP\n\n● **Jira**\n- Delayed/ pending instapay\n- Non-urgent Phone calls\n\n● **Slack**\n- Reject NID (ID Identifying channel)\n### **⏱️ 2 Business Days**\n● **Dashboard**\n- Unlock Sealed Account\n- Free Card Reorder\n- Delete Account\n- Upgrade Limits\n- Swap Number\n- Release Number\n● **Jira**\n- Branch Complaint\n- 1st Top-up reactivation\n- BNPL Issue\n- Balance mismatch\n- Balance Inquiry\n- E-Wallet failed top-up\n- Failed Top-Up by Card\n- Fake Spending Limits\n- ATM fees issue\n- Failed / Delayed P2P\n- Transaction Issue\n\n**⏱️3 Business Days**\n● **Jira**\n- 1st Top-up Refund\n- Waffarha Voucher Non-Urgent\n- Subscription Delivery\n- Mixed & Card Quality\n- Proof of Payment\n- Transaction OTP\n- General Issue\n- Subscriptions Issue\n- App crash / Looping / Hang / Error\n- Billing Issue\n- Online Payment (Fawry Pay)\n- Space Issues\n- Card Activation Issue\n\n**⏱️5 Business Days**\n● **Jira**\n- Vouchers & Gift cards\n- Rewards","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["business days","cases","service level","sla","slas","time frame","urgent","المدة","الوقت","كام يوم"]},{"category": "SLAs & Urgent Cases","title": "Urgent cases","content": "**Urgent Cases**\n### **1- Waffarha Voucher Issues**\nIf a user has a Waffarha voucher issue and contacts us while they are at the branch:\n- Raise it in Jira “[Waffarha Voucher Issue](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/799)”.\n- Select the urgency as \"Urgent\".\n\n### **2- Urgent Calls**\nIf a user requests an immediate call or a manager call:\n- Raise it in Jira [“Call - Escalation](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/832)”.\n- Select the urgency as \"Urgent\".\n- SLA: 30 Minutes.\n- The Jira ticket will be reflected in the Urgent Cases Channel.\nIf you decide to call the user yourself:\n- Raise it in Jira.\n- Once it appears in the Urgent Cases Channel, change the status to \"Sync\".\n- Add your update/comment to the thread.\n\n### **3- Non-Urgent Calls**\nIf the user requests a call but it is not urgent:\n- Raise it in Jira [“Call - Escalation](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/832)”.\n- Select the urgency as \"Non-Urgent\".\n- SLA: 1 Working Day.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["cases","slas","urgent"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "Manual Release/POS Transaction","content": "**Declined & Deducted:**• If a user reports a POS transaction where the amount was deducted but the transaction was declined and has a receipt, inform the user how to raise a Manual Release request through the app.• Transaction will be through Telda card (pin) or Apple Pay or a contactless method.➡️**Steps:**\n\n1- Open the transaction (the status must be Authorized).\n2- Select Report an Issue.\n3- Choose This Transaction Failed.\n4- Upload the receipt (mandatory).➡️If the request got submitted (receipt available)\n\n•The receipt will be validated within 1 business day.\n•If the receipt is valid, the amount will be refunded after 5 working days as long as the transaction status is ‘’Authorized’’•If the transaction becomes “Completed” during those 5 business days, follow the Chargeback process (45 days).➡️If there’s no available receipt?• The transaction will auto-release after 30 days as long as the transaction status remains ‘’Authorized’’• If the transaction becomes “Completed” during those 5 business days, follow the Chargeback process (45 days).• We don’t ask users to contact the merchant using the RRN or Auth Code during processing or to request a refund if the transaction is cleared. However, if the user chooses to go back to the merchant to ask for a refund, that is their decision.\n\n➡️Information about the receipt:If the receipt shows that the transaction was declined due to **Insufficient Funds**, it is **not considered a valid receipt**.\n\n➡️The receipt must contain the **date and time of the transaction**, along with **at least 2 of the following details**:\n- RRN\n- Last 4 digits of the card\n- Terminal ID\n- Transaction amount\n**This type of receipt is also considered valid, even if it does not contain the usual information.**\n**The receipt must include:**\n- Date & Time\n- Merchant Name\n- Response Code\n- STAN\n**Note:** The STAN is the last 5 digits of the RRN.\n\n**Void Transaction**A **Void Transaction** is used before the transaction is captured/settled.\n- A void message is considered an **authorization reversal**.\n- The amount should be refunded **instantly**.\nIf a user contacts us with a **Void Receipt** and the amount has not yet been reflected in their account:\n- The receipt is considered **valid** for a **Manual Release** request.\n- The Void Receipt will have the **same Auth Code** as the original transaction.\n**Example for Void Receipt below.**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["deducted declined","manual","pos","pos declined","receipt","release","transaction","transactions","void","إيصال","اتخصم","اترفض"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "ATMs Complaints","content": "**ATMs Complaints**\n\n- **BDC - Failed deposit**\n- **BDC - Reversal**\n- **BDC - Withdrawal**\n- **Faulty BDC**\n- **BDC Apple Pay**\n- **Non - BDC withdrawal**\n- **Non BDC deposit**\n- **Non BDC - Apple Pay**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["atms","complaints","transactions"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "BDC - Failed deposit","content": "**BDC - Failed deposit**\n\nIf a user reports that they made a deposit through a BDC ATM and the amount was not reflected in their account:\n- Check the Dashboard first.\nIf there is no BDC deposit transaction showing on the Dashboard, collect the following information:\n- Deposit amount\n- Date and time of the transaction\n- Phone number entered during the deposit\n- ATM IDIf the user does not know the ATM ID, ask for the ATM address and retrieve the ATM ID from the [Form BDC locator sheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1WzfpAU8pBEzn3yiMG_3uguDvIDYHg0AD/edit?gid=1187412626#gid=1187412626).\nIf the user cannot provide an accurate location or the ATM ID cannot be found:\n- Ask the user to contact **Banque du Caire Customer Service (16990)**, provide the ATM location, and request the ATM ID.\n- Or, the user can revisit the ATM, select **Check Balance**, print a receipt, and provide the receipt so the ATM ID can be identified.\n### **Escalation Process**\nOnce all required information is collected:\n- Raise a **Chargeback Request** through the Dashboard.\n- A response from BDC is expected within **3 Business Days**.\n\n**To follow up on the complaint raised for you, please follow these steps:**\n\n1- Open the Telda app.\n2- Tap on your **profile picture**.\n3- Select **Help**.\n4- You'll find the complaint listed under **Chargeback Case**.\n**Chargeback steps**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["atm deposit missing","bdc","deposit","deposit not reflected","failed","money didn't show","transactions","إيداع ماكينة","الإيداع لم يظهر","المبلغ ماوصلش"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "BDC - Reversal","content": "**BDC - Reversal**\n\nIf a user reports that they made a deposit through a BDC ATM and the amount was not reflected in their account, and there is a **BDC Reversal** transaction visible on the Dashboard:\n### **Required Information**\n- Phone number entered during the deposit.\n### **Escalation Process**\n- The phone number used during the deposit.\n- Raise a **Chargeback Request** through the Dashboard.\n### **SLA**\n- A response from Banque du Caire (BDC) is expected within **3 Business Days**.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["bdc","deposit reversed","reversal","transactions","إيداع مرتجع","استرجاع"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "BDC - Withdrawal","content": "**BDC - Withdrawal**\n\nIf a customer reports that the amount was deducted but cash was not received:\n- Raise a chargeback request following the normal process.\n- We will receive a response from the bank within **3 Business Days**.\n\n### **Chargeback Steps**\n- Press on the failed **BDC withdrawal transaction**.\n- Click **Chargeback**.\n- Fill in the required information.\n- For **Chargeback Reason**, select **\"Failed Withdrawal\"**.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["bdc","cash not received","transactions","withdraw no cash","withdrawal","الفلوس ماطلعتش","سحب","مطلعش كاش"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "Faulty BDC","content": "**Faulty BDC:****When a user reports an issue with a BDC ATM, whether for a deposit or withdrawal, please collect the following information:**\n\n1- Reassure the user that their card is working normally and that the issue is related to the BDC ATM, not the card itself.\n2- A screenshot of the error message or the ATM screen showing the issue.\n3- The ATM ID.\n- If the user does not know the ATM ID, ask for the ATM address and retrieve the ATM ID from the [Form BDC locator sheet](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1WzfpAU8pBEzn3yiMG_3uguDvIDYHg0AD/edit?gid=1187412626#gid=1187412626).\n4- The date of the transaction attempt.\n\n### **Escalation Process:**\nAfter collecting the required information:\n1- Open the [Requests Form](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdXcWsR8tiey5Q-L-fnN1NP-taLloaFDKNgWNks_g6tJriHxg/viewform?pli=1&pli=1).2- Select \"Faulty BDC ATM Report\".3- Submit the report to BDC.4- For **withdrawals**, advise the user to try another **BDC / Non BDC ATMs**.5- For **deposits**, advise the user to try another **BDC ATM** or another **cash-in/deposit method**.\n### **Important**\n- There is no SLA for these cases.\n- The report is only sent to BDC so they can investigate and resolve the ATM issue when possible.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["atm error","bdc","faulty","machine broken","transactions","الماكينة بايظة","خطأ ماكينة","ماكينة عطلانة"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "BDC - Apple Pay","content": "**BDC withdrawal - Apple Pay**\n\nApple Pay withdrawals are currently working on BDC ATMs; however, this is not a supported feature and is considered a technical issue. The team is working on preventing these transactions.\n### **Important**\n- **Do not inform customers that Apple Pay withdrawals on BDC ATMs are supported.**\n- **Advise customers not to use Apple Pay for ATM in the future and to use their physical Telda card only when withdrawing cash from ATMs.**\n### **Cash Not Received Cases**\nIf a customer reports that the amount was deducted but cash was not received:\n- Raise a chargeback request following the normal process.\n- The SLA for these cases is **10 Business Days**.\n**If a user complains about ATM fees charged while withdrawing from a BDC ATM using Apple Pay, the fees cannot be refunded**.\n### **Internal Process (For your information)**\n- The CB Team validates the case.\n- The case is then escalated for a manual reversal through Mastercard.\n- Since the case is handled through the reversal process, **manual refunds or exceptions can’t be made**, as this may result in a **duplicate refund**.\n**How to Identify a BDC Withdrawal via Apple Pay**\n- The **BDC logo will not appear** on the Dashboard.\n- The **Apple Pay logo will appear**.\n- The transaction will have the **Acquirer BIN: 009850**, which is Banque du Caire's acquirer BIN.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["apple","apple pay","bdc","pay","provisioning","transactions","wallet","ابل باي","محفظة"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "Non-BDC","content": "**Non- BDC Withdrawal**\n\nIf a customer reports that the amount was deducted but cash was not received:\n- Raise a chargeback request following the normal process.\n- We will receive a response from the bank within **5 Business Days**.\n\n### **Chargeback Steps**\n- Press on the failed Non - **BDC withdrawal transaction**.\n- Click **Chargeback**.\n- Fill in the required information.\n- For **Chargeback Reason**, select **\"Failed Withdrawal\"**.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["bdc","non","transactions"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "Non BDC - Deposit","content": "**Non - BDC deposit**\n\nIf a user complains that he deposited an amount through Non - BDC atm, **required Information from the user**\n- Date & Time\n- Amount (EGP)\n- ATM ID\n- Receipt photo (if available)\n\n### **Escalation Process**\nAfter collecting the required information, send an email to the CB team so they can contact the bank and proceed with a **Good Faith if possible**.\n\n### **Email Template**\n**To:** settlement@telda.app, chargeback@telda.app**CC:** cs@telda.app**Subject:** Non-BDC ATM Deposit\n**Body:**Kindly find the transaction details below, as the user has clarified that he deposited an amount through (Put the Bank's ATM name).\nUser ID:Date & Time:Amount: EGPATM ID:Chat link:\nBest Regards,[Agent Name]\n**SLA**\n- There is **no SLA** for these cases.\n- The CB team will contact the bank and wait for their response.\n\n### **Important**\n- Always inform the user to use **BDC ATMs only for deposits**.\n- Clarify that there is **no SLA,** as we will wait for the bank’s response and will inform the user once there is an update.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["bdc","deposit","non","non bdc deposit","other bank atm deposit","transactions","إيداع بنك تاني"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "Non BDC - Apple Pay","content": "**Non - BDC Apple Pay**\n\nIf a user reports a **withdrawal from a non-BDC ATM** where cash was not received, and the transaction is identified as **Apple Pay**, follow the process below.\n**We will raise a chargeback.**\n### **SLA (based on transaction amount)**\n- **Amounts below 350 EGP:**\n- **SLA: 5 Working Days (Proceed with an out-of-pocket refund)**\n- **Amounts above 350 EGP:**\n- **SLA: up to 45 Business Days (Initiate a Mastercard chargeback)**\n\n### **How to Identify Apple Pay & Non-BDC ATM Transaction**\n1- The **Apple Pay logo** will appear next to the transaction.2- Check the **Acquirer BIN**:\n- If it is **NOT \"009850\"**, then it is a **Non-BDC ATM transaction**.\n### **Important Notes:****Advise customers not to use Apple Pay for ATM in the future and to use their physical Telda card only when withdrawing cash from ATMs.**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["apple","apple pay","bdc","non","pay","provisioning","transactions","wallet","ابل باي","محفظة"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "Fawry Rejected deposit cases","content": "**Fawry Rejected Deposit Cases**\nWhen a user reports that they made a Fawry deposit but the amount has not been reflected in their account:\n\n**Process:**\n\n1- Ask the user to provide the Fawry deposit receipt.\n\n2- Validate the receipt.\n\n3- If the receipt is valid, raise a request through the Dashboard with an SLA of **3 working days**.\n\n**If the request is rejected/invalidated (Due to being Not found)**\n\n**To set the correct expectations, please explain the following to the user:**\n- Please note that the most likely next step is for Fawry to forward the case to their sponsor bank. Their bank begins a good-faith process, and this process may take up to 3 weeks to a month to receive a response from their side.\n\n- We understand that waiting can be challenging; however, when third parties are involved, we are required to follow their procedures.\n\n- What we can assure you is that once the amount is received on our side, it will be credited to your account immediately.\"Please use the **\"Fawry Not Found\"** canned response when handling these cases.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["cases","deposit","fawry","fawry deposit","fawry not found","rejected","transactions","إيداع فوري","فوري"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "Merchant Token","content": "**Merchant Token Transactions** This transaction does not indicate it was made via**Apple Pay.** It simply means it is linked to a merchant token (M4M token) stored by the merchant to process payments.\nIn other words, treat it as a regular online payment and follow the standard fraud claim process, not the Apple Pay fraud alert process.\n**Important note** Even if the card is locked or deactivated, the merchant may still be able to process transactions through an active M4M token.\nTo prevent future transactions through the merchant token, the M4M token **must** be removed from the Tokenization section on the dashboard.\n**FYI****(** we will not share it with the user**)** A merchant token can only be created if the card has previously been linked to the merchant or used for a transaction with them.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["merchant","token","transactions"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "Refund","content": "**Refund Process**\n\n| Refund State | 1-Refund with proof | 2-Semi Proof | 3-Refund with NO Proof |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Definition | The transaction was made using a Telda card, and the user has proof of the refund from the merchant stating the SLA. | The transaction was made using a Telda card, and the user has proof for the refund from the merchant without promised SLA. | The transaction was made using a Telda card, and has no proof that the merchant approved for a refund. |\n| Questions to Cover with the User | -Ask about how long the refund will take to be refunded -Ask for a proof or evidence stated refund SLA (message/Email) -Ask about items/services (if the transaction cleared) | -Ask about how long the refund will take to be refunded -Ask for a proof or evidence stated refund SLA (message/Email) -Ask about items/services (if the transaction cleared) | -Ask about how long the refund will take to be refunded -Ask for a proof or evidence stated refund SLA (message/Email) -Ask about items/services (if the transaction cleared) |\n| Action | If the mentioned SLA has passed and the user provides proof, we will proceed with raising a chargeback. | We have to wait for the merchant’s promised SLA before raising chargeback action. If the customer was not promised with a refund SLA, we will assume the standard offline refund SLA of 14 days. (You can raise it on the 15th) | If the user fails to provide proof that the merchant promised a refund, the case will be treated as a “Service Not Received” case with no proof. Meaning: It will be raised once the transaction clears, if it hasn’t been automatically released after the 30-day grace period. |\n\n**Important Note:**We must count the refund SLA from the refund date,not from the transaction date\n\n| Query → Online/POS Transaction → Refund Policy - Online/POS | When a user asks a general question about refunds or wants to request a refund for a transaction |\n| --- | --- |\n| Complaint → Refunds → Refund Not Received | If a user complains about not receiving a refund for a specific transaction |","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["merchant refund","refund","refund not received","transactions","استرجاع فلوس","المبلغ يرجع","ريفاند"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "Chargeback","content": "- The clearing date must be within the last 90 days.\n- We have to determine a chargeback reason.\n- We have to determine whether we’re disputing a full or partial amount.\n- If we’re disputing for fraud, it can only be online and not secured.\n- With the exception of Fraud, Double Presentment & Late Presentment, we must request evidence.\n- At any point during the chargeback cycle, the customer may refer back to the merchant and this would not affect the outcome of their chargeback request.\n- If the user intends to provide an email as evidence to raise a chargeback, please request that they print the email and send it to us as a PDF document.\n- If a user is reporting a declined POS transaction with no receipt, and you ask the user if they paid using a different card, we could have asked for the receipt or proof showing they had paid using a different means.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["chargeback","dispute","transactions","استرداد","نزاع"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "Declined Top Up","content": "**Declined Top Up**\n**We must ask the user on the bank name to make sure its not an international bank**\n**If it's a national bank, we can provide him the following:**\n- please make sure there are enough amount covered the 1% fees\n- The issuer supports online payments.\n- the  issuer supports OTP Verification (3DS)\n- User can unlink the linked Visa details then link it again\n\n**💥Please note that it's available to make only 2 successful transactions each 30 min.(****This information must not be communicated to users****)**\nThe user can try again and the maximum amount to be transferred from the Visa is **20,000 EGP** either to that account or another Telda account.If the transaction still declined we must offer alternative cash-in methods:\n**1- InstaPay2- Bank Transfer3- Transfer from another Telda user4- Deposit through Banque du Caire ATM5- Deposit through Fawry**\n**Also advise the user to contact the issuer bank, as no further action can be taken from our side regarding the decline.**\n\n## **Deducted but Declined Top-Up**\n\nIf the user reports that the amount was deducted from the Visa card and the top-up transaction was declined and has not been refunded yet\n### **Process**\n1- Ask the user to contact their bank first.\n2- If they didn’t help the user, request proof from the user, such as:\n- A screenshot from the bank's application.\n- Or any proof showing the amount was deducted.\n3- Raise a Jira ticket so the Back Office team can investigate and provide proof that the amount did not reach Telda.\n4- Once we receive a response from the Back Office, we will share this proof with the user so they can return to their bank for further follow-up.\n\n### **Jira Details**\n- **Jira Link:** [Failed Top-up by Card](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/170)\n- **SLA:** 2 Business Days","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["cant add money","declined","top","top up failed","transactions","visa declined","إضافة رصيد","الشحن فشل","مبيشحنش"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "Invalidated Chargebacks","content": "**Invalidated Chargebacks**\nIf you need to add a comment or Note to a chargeback that has already been invalidated or rejected, please send the adjustment to the chargebacks Channel using the template below, because Fin-Ops is not receiving any notifications for your comments\n\nUser ID:\nComplaint Date:\nAdjustment details:\nChat URL:","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["chargeback","chargebacks","dispute","invalidated","transactions","استرداد","نزاع"]},{"category": "Transactions","title": "Instapay","content": "**Instapay**\n\nWe can now view **Pending InstaPay transfers** on the Dashboard.\n### **What does \"Pending InstaPay\" mean?**\nA Pending InstaPay transaction means that the transfer was **successfully sent from InstaPay**, but the transaction is delayed on our side and appears as a **Pending** transaction on the Dashboard.\n### **Process**\nIf an InstaPay transfer remains **Pending for more than 15 minutes**:\n- Raise a Jira ticket under [Instapay Issue](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/71).\n- **SLA:** 1 Business Day.\n\n**InstaPay Cases & Contact Trees**\n\n**1- User asks how to transfer from InstaPay to Telda**\n- Tree: Query → Cash In → InstaPay In\n\n**2- User asks how to link Telda to InstaPay or create an InstaPay account using Telda**\n- Tree: Query → Cash Out → InstaPay\n\n**3- Pending/Late InstaPay Transfer**\n- Tree: Complaint → Cash In/Out → InstaPay Late Deposit\n\n**4- Failed InstaPay Transfer**\n- Tree: Complaint → Cash In/Out → InstaPay Failed Deposit\n\n**5- Failed InstaPay Transfer Due to Outage**\n- Tree: Complaint → Outages → InstaPay","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["instapay","instapay late","instapay pending","transactions","انستاباي","تحويل متأخر"]},{"category": "Bills, Payments & Transfers","title": "Partners","content": "**Partners**\n\n**Seven App:**\n**Seven** is a consumer finance company (similar to Souhoola / Contact).Telda is now available as a **cash-out option**, which means users can transfer/withdraw their available limit to their Telda account.\n\n### **💳 How to Link Telda Card**\n1- Click on **Add Card**.2- Select **Telda Card**.3- Add the Telda card details.\n\n### **💸 How to Transfer from Seven to Telda Card**\n1- After linking the Telda card, the user can transfer their limit:\n- Minimum: **1,000 EGP**\n- Maximum: **60,000 EGP**\n2- Enter the amount.\n3- Upload the invoice.\n4- Enter the seller’s name.\n5- Add the product name.\n6- Click **Continue** and choose the suitable installment plan.\n7- Review the terms and conditions, then enter the OTP.\n\n**Seven App – OTP Troubleshooting**\nIf the user does not receive the OTP, follow the troubleshooting steps below:\n- Ensure the user has the **same mobile number and National ID** registered on both apps.\n- Make sure both apps are **updated to the latest version**.\n- Check that the **Telda app has notification permissions enabled** and is allowed to run in the background.\n- Remove both apps and reinstall them.\n- Ask the user to try opening both apps from a different device if possible. (Not Mandatory)\nIf the user still does not receive the OTP:\n- Raise a Jira ticket under [BNPL Issue](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/167).\n\n⚠️ **Eligibility Note**\n- This feature is available **only for Egyptian users**.\n- It is not available for**foreign users**.\n➡️ **Seven Transfer Issues**\nIf a user reports that a Seven transfer has not been reflected in their Telda account:\n- Refer the user back to **Seven Support** to check the transfer status and assist further.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["bills","partners","payments","transfers"]},{"category": "Bills, Payments & Transfers","title": "Bank Transfer","content": "**Bank Transfer**\n**SLA**\n- Transfer to Account Number: Within 2 Business Days\n- Transfer to Card Number: Within 5 Business Days\n\n**Late Bank Transfer Escalation**\nIf a user reports that they made a bank transfer and the amount has not been received:\n1- Check the transfer method:\n- Transfer to Account Number → SLA: 2 Business Days\n- Transfer to Card Number → SLA: 5 Business Days\n2- If the SLA has passed and the issue is still not resolved:\nAsk the user for:\n- ACH receipt (for local transfers)\n- Swift receipt (for international transfers)\nThen raise an email to the CB team for investigation.\n\n### **Email Template**\nTo: settlement@telda.appCC: cs@telda.app\nSubject: Late bank transfer from (..............)\nBody:\nUser ID:Issue:Phone Number:Chat Link:\nAdd Attachment: ACH / Swift receipt\n\n**⏱️** **CB Team Email SLA: 3 Business Days****This SLA is for the CB team to check the issue, verify the details, and escalate it if needed.**\n**It is not a timeframe to receive a final response or resolution.**\n\n**➡️****Swift Receipt**\nHere is an example of a valid Swift receipt.\nThe format may differ from one bank to another, but it must include the required transfer information.\n\n**➡️****Swift Bank Transfer**\nIf the user cannot provide the Swift receipt, they must provide the mandatory information below before raising a complaint to the CB team.\n\n### **Transaction Information**\n- Transaction ID\n- Amount\n- Currency\n- Transfer Date\n### **Sender Information**\n- Sender Bank (including SWIFT code)\n- Sender Name\n- Sender IBAN\n### **Beneficiary Information**\n- Beneficiary Name\n- Beneficiary Account Number\n- Beneficiary Bank\n\n**➡️ACH Receipt:**\n\n**IBAN:**\nInternational transactions are currently suspended based on a decision from the Central Bank and the user can still use their card normally on any local website or app.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["bank","bills","late transfer","payments","transfer","transfer not received","transfers","التحويل ماوصلش","تحويل بنكي"]},{"category": "Bills, Payments & Transfers","title": "Bills / Online Payments","content": "**Bills / Online Payments (Fawry Pay)**\n\n**1- Bills / Online Payment complaints:**\n\n**1- Service not received:**\n\nIf a user reports that they did not receive the service, whether it is a bill payment or an online payment, please follow the steps below.\n**Ask the user to wait 48 hours.**\nIf they still do not receive the service after 48 hours, they should contact us again so we can raise a Jira ticket.**Online Payments (Fawry Pay) - Jira Escalation Update**\n**Before raising Jira for Online Payments (Fawry Pay) issues, follow these steps first:**1- Ask the user for a screenshot of the **Payment History**.\n2- Check if there is a transaction made on the same date:\n✅ If the transaction exists:\n- This means the user received the service.\n- No Jira should be raised.\n❌ If there is no transaction on the same date:\n- Raise Jira → [Online Payment (Fawry Pay)](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/240)\n⚠️ **Important Notes:**\n- Users can check the Payment History from the **website only** (example: Spotify website, not the app).\n- This extra verification step applies only to **Fawry Pay online payments**.\n- It does **not** apply to bills (Recharge, ADSL, Electricity, etc.).\n**How to Check Payment History**\n### **Spotify:**\nUsers can find the payment history by following these steps:\n1- Open the **Spotify website**.2- Log in to the account and click on the **profile picture**.3- Go to the **Payment** section and select **Payment History**.\n\n### **Netflix:**\nUsers can find the payment history by following these steps:\n1- Open the **Netflix website**.2- Select **Account** → **Membership**.3- Under **Payment Info**, select **View Payment History**.\n\n**2- Pending Transaction:**\nIf a user reports that they did not receive the service and the transaction status is **Pending** on the Dashboard:\n- Raise a Jira ticket directly.\n\n**Escalations:**\n\n[Online Payment (Fawry Pay)](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/240)**→** SLA 3 WD\n\n[Billing Issue](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/239)**→** SLA 3 WD\n**2- Errors:**\n### **1- Provider Error**\nWhen a user tries to pay a bill and receives a **\"Provider Error\"**:\n- Advise the user to try again later.\n- Make sure the user is completing the payment process correctly.\nIf there is a high volume of Provider Errors:\n- Collect samples and report the issue internally.\n⚠️ **Important:**Do not mention the provider name (**Fawry / Sahl / Superpay**) to the user.The provider name should only be used for internal complaints.\n**2- Identifier Error**\nThis means the user entered incorrect bill details.\nAdvise the user to:\n- Check the entered details.\n- Try again.\n\n## **3- Bill Payment Icons**\nThe icons indicate the payment method:\n💸 **Cash Icon:** Paying fully using Telda card.\n💳 **Card Icon:** Paying fully using an external card.\n⚫ **Points Icon:** Paying fully using points.\n⚫ + 💸 **Points + Cash Icons:** Paying using both points and Telda card.\n\n**If a user pays a bill using an external card:**\n- The transaction will appear only in the Bills section.\n- It will not appear in the Transactions section, as it only records financial activity that affects the Telda account balance.\nYou can also check the transaction details and find the applied fees under the External Card section.\n\n## **➡️ Remove Saved Bills**\n1- Press on the **3 dots**.2- Select **Bills**.3- Tap **Edit**.4- Press on the **\"-\"** icon.5- Select **Delete** to remove the saved bill.\n\n**➡️ADSL Bill Payment – Duplicate**\nIf a user makes an **ADSL bill payment** and the amount is deducted twice with the same amount:\n- Two deducted transactions will appear on the Dashboard.\n- Confirm with the user that the bill payment was completed successfully.\nAdvise the user to check their balance on their **WE account**, as the second deducted amount should be added back there and can be used to pay the next month's bill.\n\n**Online Payment**\n\n**Spotify:**\n### **Android Users**\nTo subscribe to Spotify:\n1- Open the **Spotify app** and tap **Premium**.2- Choose the preferred plan and tap **\"One-time payment\"**.3- Select the subscription duration, then tap **Continue**.4- Choose **Fawry** as the payment method and enter your mobile number.5- Copy the reference number that appears.6- Open the **Telda app → Online Payments → Spotify → Paste the code**.\nThe amount will be deducted from the Telda account, and the Spotify subscription will be activated.\n\n### **iOS Users**\niOS users need to complete the subscription through the **Spotify website**, as they can’t complete it directly from the Spotify app.\n\n⚠️ **Important Note**\nSpotify offers cannot be used with Telda, as they require a **credit card**.\n**Shahid:**\nTo subscribe to Shahid using Telda:\n1- Open [Shahid](https://shahid.mbc.net/en)[ ](https://shahid.mbc.net/en)from your browser and sign in to your Shahid account.2- Click **Subscribe** and choose your preferred plan.3- **Fawry payment** is available only for the **yearly** or **3-month plans**. To activate it, click **Apply** above the plan next to the offer.4- After selecting **Fawry** as the payment method, click **Pay**. A reference number will appear — copy it.5- Open the **Telda app → Online Payments → Shahid → Paste the code**.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["bill not paid","bills","fawry pay","online","payments","spotify netflix shahid","transfers","خدمة","فاتورة","مدفوعات"]},{"category": "Bills, Payments & Transfers","title": "Service not Received (Online Transaction)","content": "**Service not Received (Online Transaction)**\n\n| Transaction Status | Processing | Cleared |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Questions to be asked | - Have you tried reaching out to their support team to demand a refund? - What was their response? - Do you have your conversation with the merchant documented? If there are emails please print them out and send the PDF version - Please provide us with the item/service description you were paying for. - Do you have pictures of the faulty product? - Do you have documentation that service was not given? | - Have you tried reaching out to their support team to demand a refund? - What was their response? - Do you have your conversation with the merchant documented? If there are emails please print them out and send the PDF version - Please provide us with the item/service description you were paying for. - Do you have pictures of the faulty product? - Do you have documentation that service was not given? |\n| Notes | We will no longer ask users to contact the merchant using the RRN and Auth Code during processing. | -Before raising the CB, we must ask the above questions.  -The customer has the right to dispute a transaction even without evidence  -The only case where users may be advised to contact the merchant is after the transaction has cleared, and only for trusted online merchants  -During the chargeback period, the customer may refer back to the merchant to demand a refund if they want to. |\n\n| Reply | For now the transaction is still on-hold. This means the amount has not been transferred to the merchant's bank yet. As long as the transaction status remains authorized it will automatically be reversed after 30 days. If the transaction status changes to “completed” during this 30-day period, you can reach out to us to submit a chargeback request. Once submitted, the process can take up to 45 days for a response from the merchant’s bank. | We raised a chargeback request to MasterCard. This is done to dispute the transaction on your behalf. - The merchant's bank has up to 45 days to respond. That doesn't mean it will always take that long, but it's the maximum allowed. - At the end of the 45-day period, if the merchant cannot prove the charge was valid, the money is refunded to your account. |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n\n**Online Transaction - Service not received**\n\n**When a user complained that he had made an online transaction, but the amount was deducted and the service was not received:****1- Transaction Status - Processing / Authorized:**\n**Agent Guidelines & Actions:**\n\n- **Do not** ask users to contact the merchant using the RRN and Auth Code.\n- Explain the 30-day process (transaction remains authorized, amount releases/refunds after this period).\n- Explain the 45-day Chargeback process in case the status changes to Completed.\n**Questions to Ask**: None required at this stage\n**Response:** For now, the transaction is still on hold, which means the amount has not been transferred to the merchant’s bank yet. As long as the transaction status remains Authorized, it will be automatically reversed after 30 days.\n\nIf the transaction status changes to **Completed** during these 30 days, you can contact the merchant using the RRN (you can find it by opening the transaction in the Telda app) and request a refund, since the amount was deducted but the service was not received.\n\nIf the merchant does not help and asks you to contact us, please provide:\n\n- Screenshot of the merchant’s response.\n- Screenshot from the merchant’s app/website showing that there was no transaction on the same date (Telda transaction date).\n\nThen you can raise a complaint from the Telda app:\n\n1- Open the transaction.\n2- Click Report an Issue.\n3- Select the relevant issue.\n4- Confirm the terms.\n5- Submit the request.\n\nOnce submitted, the process can take up to 45 days for a response from the merchant’s bank.\n\n**2- Transaction Status - Cleared / Completed:**\n\n**Agent Guidelines & Actions:**\n- You must ask the required questions before raising the CB.\n\n- Only advise users to contact the merchant if it is a trusted online merchant.\n\n**Questions to Ask the User:**\n- Have you tried contacting the merchant’s support team and requesting a refund?\n- What was the merchant’s response?\n- Do you have any documented conversation with the merchant?\n- If you have emails, please print them and send the PDF version.\n- Please provide the item/service description you paid for.\n- Do you have pictures of the faulty product (if applicable)?\n- Do you have any proof that the service was not received?\n**Response:**\nWe have raised a chargeback request with Mastercard to dispute the transaction on your behalf.\n\nThe merchant’s bank has up to 45 days to respond. This does not mean it will always take the full period, but this is the maximum allowed timeframe.\n\nAt the end of the 45 days, if the merchant can’t prove that the transaction was valid, the amount will be refunded to your account.\n\n**To follow up on the complaint raised for you, please follow these steps:**\n1- Open the Telda app.\n2- Tap on your **profile picture** (top right corner).\n3- Select **Help**.\n4- You'll find the complaint listed under **Chargeback Case**.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["bills","did not receive","not","online","payments","received","service","service not received","transaction","transfers","الخدمة ماوصلتش","مستلمش الخدمة"]},{"category": "Bills, Payments & Transfers","title": "Transportation Cases","content": "**🚍****Transportation Cases**\n\n## **1- Pre-Authorization**\nIf a user reports that they have not received a refund from transportation apps (e.g., **Uber, Didi, etc.**) and:\n- The transaction was made on the same day.\n- The transaction status is still **Processing**.\nAsk the user:\n1- Did you request a ride and then cancel it?2- Will there be any cancellation fees?\n### **If the user confirms the ride was cancelled (Confirmed whether the user cancelled the ride or the driver did):**\nExplain:\nTransportation apps like Uber, Didi, and other similar apps may deduct the amount before the captain accepts the ride. This is only to confirm that there is enough balance available on the card.\nThe amount will be refunded as long as the trip was cancelled.\nAdvise the user that they can:\n- Wait for the transportation app to process the refund, or\n- Contact the merchant and provide the **RRN** (transaction reference number) to check how long the refund will take.\n\n### **If the user confirms there is a cancellation fee:**\nExplain that the transportation app will deduct the cancellation fee and refund the remaining amount.\nExample: In this transaction, a **cancellation fee of 10 EGP** was applied. The original transaction amount was **125.1 EGP**, so Didi only charged the cancellation fee and refunded the remaining amount (**115.1 EGP**) back to the user's balance.\nYou can confirm this by checking that the transaction status is**Cleared and shown in orange**.\nWe should inform the user that the transportation app deducted only the cancellation fee and refunded the remaining amount to their balance. You can also explain the balance before and after the refund to confirm the details with the user.\n\n**2- Unknown Transportation Transaction**\n**Trip fares may change due to route changes or pricing adjustments, so the merchant may charge additional amounts later.**\nIf a user reports that they do not recognize a transportation transaction, ask:\n- Did you have any pending transportation transactions?\n- Have you checked your trip history?\n- Have you contacted the merchant to verify or clarify the charge?\n### **If the user has not contacted the merchant:**\nAsk them to contact the merchant and provide the **RRN** of the transaction for further clarification.\n### **If the user confirms the transaction is fraudulent:**\nProceed with the **Fraud Process**.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["bills","cases","payments","pre auth","ride refund","transfers","transportation","uber didi careem","اوبر","رحلة","مواصلات"]},{"category": "Bills, Payments & Transfers","title": "Instashop","content": "**Instashop** order won't appear on the dashboard (doesn't withdraw the authorized amount) unless they confirm the available merchant stock, as the products you ordered might be out of stock. Once available stock is confirmed only then the transaction is authorized = shown on the dashboard.\n**Does this mean the transaction will appear right away on BD?**\nNo, transactions will only appear after stock confirmation and successful authorization.\n**Does this mean the order wouldn't be marked as successful on Instashop till the authorization happens?**\nNo, the order will be marked as successful on Instashop even before authorization as a sign that it's being worked on, not that the order is successfully paid for.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["bills","instashop","payments","transfers"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Card Related","content": "**Premium Users: Non-BDC Withdrawal Fees**\n- Each premium user has 3 free Non-BDC withdrawals each calendar month. Please note that refunded transactions do not count toward these 3 free withdrawals.\n- For example: If a user has 3 refunded Non-BDC transactions, they will still have 3 free Non-BDC withdrawals available.\n- If fees are Incorrectly charged in such cases, please inform the user that the fees will be refunded, and the case will be raised on Jira.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["card","cards","related"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Telda cards features","content": "**💳****Telda Cards Features**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["cards","features","telda"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Invalid Pin / Change card pin","content": "**Change card pin**\n**If a user reports that they forgot their card PIN code, send the following steps:**\n### **Standard Card:**\n**1- Open the Card Section from the home screen.2- Click on Reset PIN.3- Enter the 8-digit code on the back of the card.4- Set a new PIN for your card and confirm it.**\n\n### **Premium / Plus Card:**\n**1- Open the Card Section from the home screen.2- Click on Reset PIN.3- Enter the last 4 digits of the card number.4- Set a new PIN for your card and confirm it.**\n\n**\"Invalid PIN - Capture card\" Error**\n\nIf a user reports that they cannot pay with their card even though they have enough balance, and the Dashboard shows failed transactions with the error: **\"Invalid PIN - Capture Card\"**\n\nFollow the below:\n- Inform the user to **change the card PIN**.\n- This happens because the user entered the wrong PIN code **3 times**, which caused the card to be temporarily blocked.\n- After changing the PIN, the card will be reactivated and the user can try using the card again.\n⚠️ **Important Notes:**\n- Do **not** raise a Jira complaint as **\"Soft Blocked\"**.\n- Make sure the user follows the correct steps to change the card PIN.\n\n**Tree:**\n**Complaint → Account related → Soft Blocked → Resolved**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["card","cards","change","forgot pin","invalid","pin","reset pin","wrong pin","الباسورد بتاع الكارت","نسيت الرقم السري"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Card stuck at the ATM","content": "**Card Stuck Inside ATM**\n**If a user reports that their card is stuck inside an ATM:**\n1- **Lock the card** to prevent anyone from using it.\n2- Explain to the user how to lock the card from the app, so they can take this action if the card gets stuck again or if it is lost.\n3- Inform the user to order a new card and explain that the re-order fee is **99 EGP**.\n- If the user complains about the card fees:\n- Raise a **Free Card Reorder** request.\n- Inform the user that the request has been raised and the concerned team will review it and respond within **2 working days**.\n⚠️ **Important:**\n- If the request is raised without asking the user to order a new card first, it will be rejected.\n\n### **Contact Tree:**\n**If Free Card Reorder****is raised:**Request → Card Related → Free Card Reorder → Third Party\n**If Free Card Reorder** **is not raised:**Complaint → Card Related → Card Stuck Inside ATM → Resolved\nIf there is an issue related to **withdrawal or deposit**, raise a **CB** and select the normal contact tree based on the chargeback type.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["atm","atm ate card","card","card stuck atm","cards","stuck","the","الكارت اتعلق","الكارت في الماكينة"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Lost Card","content": "**Lost Card**\n\nIf a user reports that they found a lost Telda card, follow these steps:\n1- Ask the user to provide a **photo showing the card number** (photo of the backside of the card) so the BO team can search and identify the cardholder account.\n2- Raise Jira → [Lost Card](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/171)\n3- Inform the user that:\n- We will lock the card.\n- We will contact the cardholder to inform them that their card has been locked.\n- We will guide them on how to order a new card.\n4- Thank the user for reporting the card.\n\n⏱️ **SLA: 2 Working Days**The BO team will lock the card and contact the cardholder.\n**Contact Tree:**Request → Card related → Lock card → Resolved","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["card","cards","found card","lost","lost card","كارت ضايع","لقى كارت"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Card Activation Issues","content": "**New Process for Standard Users Facing Card Activation Issues**\nWhen a Standard user is trying to activate their card and the card status is “Card Ready for Pickup”, follow the steps below:\n1. Use Free Card Reorder\n- Select Free Card Reorder.\n- Add the chat link.\n- Once the request is approved, update the card status to Ready for Activation.\n\n2. Ask the user to refresh\n- Ask the user to close and reopen the app.\n- and provide the card activation steps.\n**Important Checks Before Proceeding**\n- KYC Status: Make sure the user has completed and signed the KYC.\n- iOS Standard Users: iOS Standard users do NOT need to pay the 50 EGP deposit.\n- Failed Top-up (Sanction Icon): If you check the sanction icon and see Top-up User Failed:\n- Ask the user to make their first top-up (50 EGP).\n- After that, they can proceed with card activation.\n- We must also ask the user for the mobile number and the NID they provided at the branch to receive the card.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["activate card","activation","cant activate card","card","cards","issues","الكارت مش متفعل","تفعيل الكارت"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Blocked by BDC","content": "**Blocked by BDC:We have two scenarios:**\n\n- The user received a message from BDC stating that their card is blocked.\n\n- The user contacted us complaining that they cannot use the card.\n\n**In both cases, if we check the processor balance, we will find a red dot.****Then, we will submit a free card reorder. The BO team will validate and approve the request with an SLA of 2 working days.Complaint > Account status > Blocked By BDC**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["bdc","blocked","cards"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Premium\\Plus","content": "**Premium/Plus card printing process:**\n- Card printing will start only after the user signs the KYC.\n- The delivery SLA starts from the date the KYC is signed.\n- The fees will be deducted before printing once the user selects the plan, but the card will not be printed until the KYC is signed.\n- The user will see a disclaimer stating that the card will be delivered within 7 business days after signing the KYC.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["cards","plus","premium"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Split Transaction Feature","content": "**Split Transaction Feature:**\n-Split Transaction Feature:\n-Single Split per Transaction: Each transaction can now only be split once.\n-Detailed Split Breakdown: See the state of each split request directly on the transaction details screen.\n-New “Split Transactions” Section: Find all your split expenses in a new dedicated section next to P2P Requests.\n-so now the transaction can be split by any amount not equally\n-Also there’s an option to cancel the split","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["cards","feature","split","transaction"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Declined Reason","content": "| Declined Reason | Investigation Needed | Action |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Invalid PIN - Capture Card | N/A | Ask user to reset Card’s PIN OR ask BO team to reset the PIN from their side |\n| Card is temporary blocked | Check Processor balance to make sure if it is blocked by BDC or not/ check account status (blocked activity-blocked KYC)\\ check card is active or not | -If it is blocked by BDC then make new card reorder -if the card is not active due to the subscription plan is terminated as user to resume the plan or request a new card as he wish -if the account is blocked make the appropriate action depends on the case |\n| Invalid PIN | N/A | Ask user to reset the PIN |\n| Card Stolen | Check if the user has 2 cards one canceled and other active | Ask the user about the card’s last 4 digits he’s using to make sure he’s using the active card |\n| Exceed Limit | Check account’s daily and monthly limits | If the user has a full profile and he’s has a sufficient limits and gets exceed monthly limits raise it JIRA as fake limit case |\n| Insufficient Fund | Check user’s balance | Ask him to make deposit first and provide him with our deposit methods |\n\n**Important notes:1-If the transaction is not shown on the dashboard and the user is complaining that he cannot make a POS transaction, we should ask whether he is using the contactless feature or the PIN.**\n**If he confirms that he is using contactless, then check whether the user has made any transaction using the PIN code after activating the card or not.2- If the transaction is using the PIN or contactless and he has already used this feature before, and there is no declined transaction on the dashboard, ask him to reset the PIN and try another merchant. If the transaction gets declined, confirm with him to capture the error then contact us again.**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["cards","declined","reason"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Card subscription","content": "**Card subscription**\n\n- **Card canceled by Bosta**\n- **Reject Premium Card Design**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["card","cards","subscription"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Card canceled by Bosta","content": "**Card canceled by Bosta**\n\n**When a user reports that Bosta cancelled the card, or when you check the Bosta tracking link and confirm that the card status is marked as cancelled**, we will raise a Jira request to redeliver it **within 7 Working days**. **The card will be delivered to the user's address only.**\n\n**We no longer deliver cards to branches.**\n\n**To proceed with the request, please ask the user for:**\n\n1- The full address in detail\n2- The phone number\n\n**Jira Link → “**[Subscription Delivery](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/250)**”**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["bosta","bosta cancelled","canceled","card","cards","redeliver card","بوسطة","توصيل كارت"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Reject Premium Card Design","content": "**Reject Premium Card Design**\n\n**We need to understand the meaning of each card status to know whether it is valid to raise the request or not.**\n\n**1- In Ops Review:**\n\nThis means the card has a design, but it has not been approved or rejected yet. At this stage, we can raise a rejection request.\n\n**2- Pending KYC:**\n\nThis means the design has already been approved, or the user submitted the card without a design, or it is a transparent card. At this stage, we cannot raise a rejection request.\n\n**3- Ordered:**\n\nThis means the card design has been approved and the user has signed the KYC. Therefore, it is also not possible to raise a rejection request at this stage.\n\n**If the card status is “In Ops Review,” we will use the template below to raise the request.**\n\nRequest Title: Reject Premium card design\n[@Mohamed Hesham](https://teldaapp.slack.com/team/U04FS8XCE14)[ ](https://teldaapp.slack.com/team/U04FW0STZGD)[@Aya Mahmoud](https://teldaapp.slack.com/team/U04FW0STZGD)\nUser ID:Chat Link:\n\n- **It's a must to mention Aya and Hisham**\n- **Request will be raised on ID identifying Channel with SLA 2 Hours of a business day**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["card","cards","design","premium","reject"]},{"category": "Cards","title": "Card reorder","content": "**Card Reorder Fees**\n\n**1- Standard Card Re-order**\nIf a user has a Standard card and wants to order a new Standard card:\n1- The user needs to deposit 99 EGP (new card order fees).\n2- Follow these steps:\n- Open the Card Section in the Telda app.\n- Click on \"Order a new Card\" (this will permanently disable the current card).\n- Click Continue to complete the request.\nAfter ordering the card, the user can visit the nearest branch to pick it up.\n\n**2- Plus / Premium Card Re-order:**\n\nIf a user is ordering a Plus/Premium card for the first time (whether as a new user choosing it as their first card or an existing Standard card holder upgrading to Plus/Premium for the first time):\n- The app will deduct only the subscription fee.\n- No card fee will be charged.\n\nIf a user already has a Plus/Premium card and wants to reorder a new one:\n- The app will deduct the card fee (99 EGP).\n- The subscription fee will also be deducted if it is due.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["card","cards","order new card","reorder","اطلب كارت","كارت جديد"]},{"category": "Apple Pay","title": "Apple Pay","content": "[Apple Pay Slides](https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1kDG94MqYBXGP_1MGoqldZfri4mHsdDGKYpvALz-7eyc/edit?slide=id.g36ce4b9ca7f_0_0#slide=id.g36ce4b9ca7f_0_0)\n\n**Apple Pay**\nIt is a **mobile payment and digital wallet service** by Apple that allows users to make secure payments in stores, apps, and websites using their **iPhone, Apple Watch, iPad, or Mac**\n\n**Tokenization**\n**Tokenization is the process of replacing sensitive data with a non-sensitive equivalent, called a token, that has no intrinsic value or meaning. This process is used to protect sensitive information, such as card numbers.**\n\n**A user can add their Telda card to Apple Pay through one of the following methods:****1- Manual Provisioning**\n- Open the **Wallet** app.\n- Tap **+**.\n- Enter the card details manually.\n### **2- Wallet Extension (\"From Apps on your iPhone\")**\n- Select **\"From Apps on your iPhone\"**.\n- Choose **Telda**.\n- Enter the Telda passcode.\n- Continue with the provisioning process.\n### **3- Telda App**\n- Add the card directly through the Telda app.\n\n**The Wallet App provisioning steps:**\n\n**To Add Your Card Using iPhone (Wallet Provisioning):**\n\n- **Open the Wallet app on your iPhone.**\n- **Tap the “+” (Add Card) button.**\n- **Choose a previous card to quickly add cards that have already been used in your wallet, or add a new debit or credit card.**\n- **Enter or confirm your card details if required.**\n- **Review and accept the Terms and Conditions to proceed.**\n- **Complete the verification process by entering the required verification OTP.**\n**The Telda app:**\n\n**How to Link Apple Pay through the Telda App:**\n\n- **Tap the “Add to Apple Pay” icon in the card section.**\n- **Enter your Telda card’s expiry date.**\n- **Enter the 6-digit verification code (OTP) sent to your registered phone number.**\n- **Review and agree to the Terms and Conditions.**\n- **Tap “Use as default card” if you’d like to make it your primary payment method.**\n\n**Note: You may be asked to provide your National ID number, date of birth, or both.**\n\n**Provisioning Flows**\n**Apple uses color-coded risk levels for provisioning attempts. Each color indicates the required verification level.**\n### **🟢 Green Flow**\n- **The safest provisioning flow.**\n- **Minimal checks are performed.**\n- **No OTP verification is required.**\n### **🟡 Yellow Flow**\n- **Provisioning will succeed.**\n- **OTP verification will be required.**\n\n### **🟠 Orange Flow**\n- **Indicates that the provisioning attempt triggered Apple’s high-risk model.**\n- **Additional verification is required.**\n- **BO will contact the user to complete the verification.**\n**Use Script:**\n**\"Kindly note that one of our team members will reach out to you to assist you with completing your linking attempt.\"**\n\n### **🔴 Red Flow**\n- **Indicates that the device score is 1 for any reason.**\n### **1- Red Due to \"Too Many Cardholders\"**\n**If the reason is related to maximum DPAN/APAN limits:**\nAdvise the user:\n*\"Kindly remove one of your cards to be able to link the new one, as the linking attempt failed due to having too many active cards.\"*\n- If the user requests it, you can remove any visible card from the app.\n### **2- Red Due to Other Reasons**\nReview the Red Reason Code **(A screenshot will be provided)**\n\n**Script**\n**English:**\n*Unfortunately, the card cannot be added to Apple Pay at the moment. Kindly try again later.*\n**Arabic:**\n*نعتذر* *لك* *جدا**ً،**ولكن* *لا* *يمكن* *ربط* *الكارت* *الخاص* *بك* *بخدمة* *أبل* *باي* *في* *الوقت* *الحالي**.**يرجى* *المحاولة* *مرة* *أخرى* *في* *وقت* *لاحق**.*\n\n**Provisioning Issues:**\n**Wallet Provisioning – Pending Verification**\n**When a user tries to provision their card through the Wallet app but:**\n- Does not receive the OTP and switches to Hotline Verification, or\n- Selects Hotline Verification from the beginning, but the verification is not completed.\n**In these cases, the card will remain in a Pending Verification status.**\n\n**Advise the user to follow these steps:**\n1- Tap the exclamation mark in the top-right corner of the card screen.\n2- Scroll down and select Remove Card.\n3- Open the Telda app and link the card again from there.\n\n**Wallet Provisioning – \"From Apps on your iPhone\" Error**\n\nWhen this error appears, it means the user is trying to provision the card through:\n**\"From Apps on your iPhone\" → Select Telda**\n\n### **Process**\n**Advise the user to provision the card by using one of the following methods instead:**\n1- Through the Wallet app using **Manual Card Entry**.\nOR\n2- Through **the Telda app** directly.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["apple","apple pay","pay","provisioning","wallet","ابل باي","محفظة"]},{"category": "Apple Pay","title": "Apple Pay Provisioning Troubleshooting","content": "For users who fail to provision their Telda card on Apple Pay and receive an error, follow the troubleshooting steps below:\n1- Go to **Settings > General > Date & Time.** Ensure **Set Automatically** is turned **ON**.\n2- Go to **Settings > General > VPN & Device Management** (or **Settings > VPN**)\n- Ensure the VPN status is **Not Connected**.\n- If possible, temporarily remove the VPN profile during setup.\n3- Go to **Settings > General > Language & Region.** Ensure the **Region** is set to **Egypt**.\n\n**If the issue persists, please verify the following:**\n1- Go to **Settings > [Customer Name] > Media & Purchases > View Account > Country/Region.** Confirm that the country/region is set to **Egypt**.\n2- Go to **Settings > [Customer Name] > Personal Information**\n- Verify the **date of birth.**\n- The user must be **over 13 years old**, as child accounts cannot add payment cards.\n3- Go to **Settings > [Customer Name] > Sign-In & Security.** Ensure **Two-Factor Authentication is** **enabled**.\n**Final Troubleshooting Step** **(Not Mandatory)**\nGo to **Settings > [Customer Name] > Sign Out**\n- Sign out of the Apple ID.\n- Restart the device.\n- Sign back in.\n**Important:** Do not perform this step if you do not remember your iCloud password.\n\n1- اذهب إلى: الإعدادات > عام > التاريخ والوقت, وتأكد من أن خيار **\"****التعيين** **تلقائي****ً****ا****\"** مفعل.\n\n2- اذهب إلى: الإعدادات > عام > VPN وإدارة الجهاز (أو الإعدادات > VPN)\n\n- تأكد من أن حالة الـ VPN هي **غير** **متصل**.\n- يفضل حذف ملف الـ VPN مؤقتًا أثناء عملية الإعداد.\n\n3- اذهب إلى: الإعدادات > عام > اللغة والمنطقة, وتأكد من أن **المنطقة** مضبوطة على **مصر**.\n\nإذا استمرت المشكلة، يرجى التحقق من التالي:\n\n1- اذهب إلى: الإعدادات > [اسم المستخدم] > الوسائط والمشتريات > عرض الحساب > الدولة/المنطقة, وتأكد من أن الدولة/المنطقة مضبوطة على **مصر**.\n\n2- اذهب إلى: الإعدادات > [اسم المستخدم] > المعلومات الشخصية\n- تحقق من تاريخ الميلاد.\n- يجب أن يكون عمر المستخدم أكثر من 13 عامًا، حيث لا يمكن للحسابات الخاصة بالأطفال إضافة بطاقات دفع.\n3- اذهب إلى: الإعدادات > [اسم المستخدم] > تسجيل الدخول والأمان, وتأكد من أن **المصادقة** **الثنائية****(****Two****-****Factor** **Authentication****)** مفعلة.\n\n**الخطوة** **الأخيرة** **(Not Mandatory)**\n\nاذهب إلى: الإعدادات > [اسم المستخدم] > تسجيل الخروج\n\n- قم بتسجيل الخروج من حساب Apple ID.\n- أعد تشغيل الجهاز.\n- قم بتسجيل الدخول مرة أخرى.\n**مهم****:** لا تقم بهذه الخطوة إذا كنت لا تتذكر كلمة مرور iCloud الخاصة بك.\n**Provisioning Issue Escalation**\n### **If the Issue Persists After Troubleshooting**\nAsk the user for the following details:\n- Device Model\n- iOS Version\n- Telda App Version\n**Note:** These details can also be checked from the Dashboard.\n\n**Raise a Complaint**\nRaise the complaint on the [Apple Pay Support Channel](https://teldaapp.slack.com/archives/C09P1PPQQ5T)**(Slack)** using the following format:\n**Provisioning Issue**\nUser ID:Provisioning Source (In App / Wallet):Device Model:iOS Version:Issue Details:App Version:Attachment (Screenshot):Freshchat Link:\n\n⚠️ **Important:**There is no SLA for Apple Pay provisioning complaints. Do not provide any SLA to the user.\n\n**Apple Pay - Card Color Issue**\nIf users report that their card color appears as **black** instead of the actual card color (**Pink, Blue, Yellow, or Transparent**) on the Wallet App:\n➡️ Remove the card from the Wallet app and provision it again.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["apple","apple pay","cant add card apple pay","pay","provisioning","provisioning error","troubleshooting","wallet","ابل باي","محفظة","مش بيتضاف ابل باي"]},{"category": "Rewards, Vouchers & Gift Cards","title": "Rewards & Vouchers","content": "**Rewards / Vouchers / Telda Shops**\n\n**Rewards:**\n### **Reward Eligibility:** Rewards apply to **purchase transactions only**.\nThe reward does **not** apply to:\n❌ Transfers or top-ups (including credit/internet for any network)❌ Bill payments (electricity, gas, internet, mobile)❌ Websites such as Amazon, Noon, Jumia and Fawry\n⚠️ The user must **activate the reward before making the transaction**.\nUsers can check the reward terms and conditions through the app:\n**Profile icon → Help → Telda Features → Reward → Terms & Conditions**\n### **Excluded Merchants:**\n- Stripe\n- Vodafone Cash\n- Etisalat Cash\n- MyFawry\n- Klivvr\n- Opay\n- Nexta\n- Noon\n- Telda\n- Jumia\n- Amazon\n- Orange\n- WE Telecom\n- Money Fellows\n\n### **Important Notes:**\n- Each reward has an expiry date, but we do **not communicate the expiry date** to users.\n- Currently, rewards appear to users without an expiry date, which means they are available for a limited time only.\n- **\"Eligible Merchant Reward\"** follows the same terms and conditions as **\"Any Purchase Reward\"**.\n\n**Cashback / Reward was not applied:**\n### 1- Check Reward Activation Status:\n**Go to:**\nTransaction → Reward Tracker\nCheck if the reward was active **before or at the transaction time**.\n\n- If the reward status shows \"**After transaction time**\":\n- This means the user activated the reward after completing the transaction.\n- Inform the user that the reward is still available on their account as long as it appears in the Dashboard and Reward section.\n- Remind the user to activate the reward before making the transaction.\n\n### 2- Check Rerun Option:\nIf the \"Rerun\" option is available for the transaction, click on it.\n\n### 3- If Reward Is Still Not Applied:\nAsk the user for a receipt:\n- POS receipt, or Order/place receipt. The user can provide either one.\n\n4- Raise Jira → [Rewards](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/245) / SLA → 5 Working Days\n⚠️ Note:If the user does not have a receipt, raise the Jira ticket normally. The BO team will validate the ticket.\n\n**Vouchers**\n**Talabat Vouchers:**\n### **How to Redeem:**\nThe user must redeem the voucher from the **Talabat app** and **should not add it to the checkout page.**\n**Steps:**\n1- Open the **Talabat app**.2- Go to **Vouchers**.3- Click **\"Get a code?\"**4- Enter the code shown in the Telda app.\n\n### **Important Notes:**\nTalabat vouchers do not apply to:\n❌ Talabat Mart❌ Hidden Gems❌ Merchants who do not accept vouchers\nError: **\"Voucher not applicable on this vendor\"**\n\n### **Voucher Expiry Date:**\n- From our side, vouchers are valid from **1 to 6 months**.\n- The user can always check the exact expiry date directly on the voucher in the Telda app.\n- If the user does not redeem the voucher, it remains valid until the expiry date shown in the app.\nOnce the user redeems the voucher with the merchant (Talabat), the merchant’s expiry rules apply.\n⚠️ **If the voucher expires after being redeemed, it is no longer valid and cannot be raised as an issue from our side.**\n**Example:**If a user purchases a Talabat voucher, they can keep it without redeeming it until the expiry date shown in the Telda app. After redeeming it on Talabat, the validity follows Talabat’s terms (**7- days)**.\n\n⚠️ **Talabat Specific Note:**\nDo **not communicate the 7-day validity period** to users.\nThe user can check the voucher's validity directly from Talabat, as Talabat provides the expiration date in its voucher section.\nIf the user complains that after redeeming the code, the active tab shows the voucher is valid for only 7 days:\nInform the user:\n**English:**Please note that the expiration date shown from our side is not related to the validity period inside the Talabat app. The date shown on our side is simply the last date you can use the code on the Talabat app. Once you redeem it, the voucher validity inside the Talabat app is subject to Talabat’s terms and conditions.\n**Arabic:**برجاء العلم ان تاريخ انتهاء الكود من خلالنا ليس له علاقة بمدة انتهاء الكود في تطبيق طلبات، بمعنى أن تاريخ الانتهاء الخاص بنا هو آخر تاريخ يمكنك استخدام الكود فيه على تطبيق طلبات. بمجرد استخدام الكود، تكون مدة صلاحية الكود داخل تطبيق طلبات حسب شروط وأحكام طلبات.\n\n## **Errors:**\n### **1- Error: \"This card is not eligible\"**\nAsk the user to:\n- Remove the Telda card from Talabat.\n- Link the card again.\n\n### **2- Error: \"This campaign reached the limit\"**\nAsk the user for:\n- Screenshot of the Talabat voucher page showing:\n- Active vouchers\n- Used vouchers\n- Expired vouchers\nCheck if the voucher amount appears under **Used / Expired** tabs:\n✅ If found:\n- Inform the user that the voucher was redeemed on Talabat.\n- Explain that Talabat mentioned the voucher expired on the date shown under the voucher amount.\n- No complaint should be raised, as there is no issue from our side.\n❌ If the voucher amount **is not found** in the three tabs:Ask the user for:\n- Screenshot of any Talabat order after purchasing the voucher.\n- The screenshot must clearly show the date and time.\nThen raise Jira → [Vouchers & Giftcards](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/244)\n⏱️ **SLA: 5 Working Days**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["cards","cashback","gift","reward not applied","rewards","voucher","vouchers","كوبون","مكافأة","نقاط"]},{"category": "Rewards, Vouchers & Gift Cards","title": "Gift cards & Vouchers","content": "**Gift cards & Vouchers**\n**We have two types of gift cards and vouchers: internal and external.**\n- **Internal Vouchers (e.g., Rabbit & Talabat)**\n- Users can purchase them using cash or redeemed points.\n- Issues should be raised JIRA FORM< SLA of 5 working days.\n\n- **External Vouchers (One Card, BME, & Like Card)**\n- Issues should be raised JIRA FORM< SLA of 5 working days.\n- We can also check the voucher type from the dashboard < details section.\n\n**Talabat Vouchers:****1- How to redeem: The user must follow the steps to redeem the voucher and not add it on the checkout page.**\n\n**2-Voucher’s expiry date**\n➡️From our side, vouchers are valid for 1 to 6 months, and the user can always check the exact expiry date directly on the voucher in the app.\nIf the user does not redeem the voucher, it will remain valid until the expiry date shown in the app.\nHowever, once the user redeems the voucher with the merchant (e.g., Talabat), the merchant’s expiry rules apply. If the voucher expires after being redeemed, it is no longer valid and cannot be raised as an issue from our side.\n**Example:**\nIf a user purchases a Talabat voucher from us, they can keep it without redeeming it for up to 6 months (depending on the date shown in the app). But if they redeem it on Talabat and it later expires, the voucher is considered expired under Talabat’s rules, and there is no issue from our side.**For Talabat, the voucher is valid for 7 days, don’t communication that to users**If we had found the voucher at the expired section we can inform the user the following:Please note that the expiration date we provide for the code is not related to its validity within the Talabat app. The date shown on our side is simply the last date you can use the code on the Talabat app. Once you redeem it, the validity of the code within the app is subject to Talabat’s terms and conditions\nبرجاء العلم ان تاريخ انتهاء الكود من خلالنا ليس له علاقة بمدة انتهاء الكود ف تطبيق طلبات , بمعني ان تاريخ الانتهاء الخاص بينا هو تاريخ انتهاء الكود بحيث تقدر تستخدمه ف تطبيق طلبات , مجرد م بتستخدمه بيكون صلاحية الكود ف تطبيق طلبات راجع ليهم\n3-Talabat vouchers are not applicable on Talabat Mart, Hidden Gems, or merchants who don’t accept vouchers.**Error: \"Voucher not applicable on this vendor\"**Advise the user to contact Talabat support for clarification.4-this card is not eligible: ask the user to remove the card then link it again.\n**5- Error: \"This campaign reached the limit\"**\nAsk the user for the following screenshots:\nTalabat voucher page (showing active, used, and expired vouchers).\nAny Talabat order after voucher purchase, with date and time clearly visible.\nThen raise it JIRA FORM with SLA 5 working days.\n\nPubg Vouchers:How to redeem:Login to your account at Midasbuy (https://www.midasbuy.com)\nAccess the “PUBG Mobile game credit Top-up” page, and enter you PUBG Mobile player ID\nAccess the “Redeem code” page, enter redemption code printed on the receipt of your purchase of this card, and enter such code on that page.\nYou can redeem this card’s value as PUBG Mobile Unknown Cash.قم بتسجيل الدخول إلى حسابك على Midasbuy (https://www.midasbuy.com) قم بالوصول إلى صفحة \"زيادة رصيد لعبة PUBG Mobile\"، وأدخل معرف لاعب PUBG Mobile الخاص بك. قم بالوصول إلى صفحة \"رمز الاسترداد\"، وأدخل رمز الاسترداد المطبوع على إيصال شراء هذه البطاقة، وأدخل هذا الرمز في تلك الصفحة. يمكنك استرداد قيمة هذه البطاقة كـ PUBG Mobile Unknown Cash\nImportant notes:1- Advise the user to use the [desktop](https://www.midasbuy.com/midasbuy/eg/redeem/pubgm?r_activity_id=Activity_1753856997_VIYJOM) view on their mobile device or on a desktop (PC or laptop) to redeem the voucher.\n2- Type the code manually instead of copying and pasting it.\n3- Make sure there are no spaces before, after, or within the code.\n4- It is mandatory to ask for a screenshot of the error before raising any voucher complaints.5-user must login to their Pubg account before redeeming the voucher\n\n**Waffaraha Vouchers****This process for Waffarha voucher complaints,**\n**We have 2 types of complaints.,**\n\n**Urgent case:** If the user has a voucher issue and contacts us while he is at the branch, we will fill out this [Jira ticket](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/799) and select its urgency as “Urgent.”\n\n**Non Urgent:** In case the user has an issue with the voucher redemption but the user left the branch or reporting an issue that doesn't need immediate action, we will raise it to [Jira](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/799), I've added the Link to the External links in Fresh Chat with the name of \"Waffarha Voucher issue\" with SLA of 3 Business days.**Waffarha voucher is** **Refundable****. (SLA 3 BD)****-** In case a user requested a refund for a voucher, we need to check the voucher expiry date, and ask for the reason. - The voucher can be refunded only while the code is valid. - If the code expired, but the user already had a complaint because they cannot redeem the voucher, we can refund them as well if they requested a refund.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["cards","gift","gift card","rewards","talabat pubg waffarha","voucher","vouchers","جيفت كارت","قسيمة"]},{"category": "Rewards, Vouchers & Gift Cards","title": "Shops","content": "**Noon Shops Discount**1-If a user is trying to use our discount code that is visible in Telda shops through the app ( FG19 ), however there is an error “” Invalid code “” :\n➡️We should ask the user first what is the category of the product that they are trying to purchase, as the code wont work in the few categories which you may find in [this sheet.](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xEbk5hwn4MvcwcXYOVbYDYcOQmctfZJ4aJocwVF-RuQ/edit?gid=1730813492#gid=1730813492)2-What if  the product is not one of the excluded list?\n➡️We can provide the user with another code to try with, out of these 3 other codes found in the below screenshot.\n💡There is a minor possibility that all codes won't work, in this case the agent can raise a ticket to BO as we will escalate it to our POC at Noon, with an SLA of 2 B.D to be resolved from their client’s side.\n\n**If the user is using the code successfully, however complaining that they received only 5 % instead of 10 % even he/she is a new user at Noon .. here is what we need to check first :-**Ask the user if this is his first order in his Noon account, and also ask about the product category.\n-Check the terms & conditions list attached below to validate if the user is eligible for compensation or not.If T & C applies, however the user received 5 % not 10 %, we will need to ask the user about their order ID/number and escalate it to BO, with an SLA of 2 working days to be compensated and resolved.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["cards","gift","rewards","shops","vouchers"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Account Related","content": "**Resume Plan**\n- Users who canceled their plan or were downgraded to the Standard plan due to insufficient balance can resume their plan at any time, as long as they have not requested a new card-If the 'Resume Plan' option is not available in the card section, we can raise it JIRA FORM**Important Notes**\n- Users can only add money to their account if their card has been activated before using one of the following methods:\n- InstaPay\n- P2P transfer\n- Bank card\n- Bank transfer\n- If the user needs to resume their plan in order to complete the signing process, they can only receive a transfer from another Telda account.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","accounts","login","related"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Resume Plan","content": "**Resume Plan**\nUsers who canceled their plan or were downgraded to the Standard plan due to insufficient balance can resume their plan at any time, as long as they have not requested a new card.\n\n### **Steps to Resume the Plan:**\n1- Open the Telda app.2- Click on the profile picture.3- Go to \"Plan\" and click \"Resume Plan\".\nAfter the fees are deducted, the card will be activated automatically.\n\n### **If \"Resume Plan\" option is not available:**\nRaise it Jira: [Subscription Issues](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/201)\n\n### **Important Notes:**\nUsers can only add money to their account if their card was activated before using one of the following methods:\n- InstaPay\n- P2P transfer\n- Bank card\n- Bank transfer\n\nIf the user needs to resume the plan to complete the signing process **(Card Order State → Pending activation)**, they can only receive a transfer from **another Telda account**.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","login","plan","reactivate plan","resume","resume plan","استئناف الاشتراك","الخطة"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Unlock Account","content": "**Unlock Account**\nWhen a user reports that their account is locked, they need to answer at least 2 of the following questions:\n1- National ID Number2- Last 4 Digits of the Card\n- If the card is lost, ask for the registered phone number instead.\n3- Subscription plan (Standard / Plus / Premium).\n\nIf the user fails to answer **2 questions correctly**, raise a **Call Request** on the **Customer Success Channel** for **Back Office validation**.User ID:Issue: Account locked - Phone Number:Chat Link:","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","account locked","accounts","login","unlock","الحساب مقفول","فتح الحساب"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Delete Account","content": "**Delete Account**\nWhen a user requests to delete their account:\n1- Ask for the reason behind the account deletion.2- Inform the user of the following:\nPlease note that after the account is deleted, the mobile number and National ID cannot be used for any other Telda account.\n3- If the user confirms the deletion request, proceed with raising the request.\nNote:\nThe account balance must be **less than 5 EGP** before raising the deletion request.\nIf the balance is more than 5 EGP, ask the user to:\n- Transfer the amount to another Telda account, or use the remaining balance.\n### **SLA**\n- Account deletion requests are completed within **2 Business Days**.\n### **Account Recovery**\nAlso inform the user:\nIf you would like to restore your account, you can contact us through our Facebook or Instagram page.\n### **Contact Tree**\n**Request → Account Related → Delete Account → Resolved**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","accounts","close account","delete","delete account","login","اقفل حسابي","حذف الحساب"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Passcode","content": "**Forgot Passcode**\nIf the user doesn’t remember the passcode and contacting us through Facebook/Instagram\n\n1. Enter your mobile number.\n\n2. Select “Forgot”.\n\n3. Enter the OTP sent to your mobile.\n\n4. Enter your National ID number.\n\n5. Set your new password.\n***A user cannot reuse a previous passcode. Once the passcode has been changed, it cannot be used again.If the user is trying to change the passcode outside the app and faced the below error, we should advise the user to try again after 24 hours from the last attempt (not less than 24 hours).**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","login","passcode"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Change Passcode","content": "**Change passcode**\n**Please follow the steps below to change the passcode on your Telda app.**\n\n1. Go to Settings.\n2. Click on Change Passcode.\n3. Enter the Current Passcode.\n4. Confirm the New Passcode.\n5. The new Passcode is ready to go.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","change","login","passcode"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Forgot Passcode","content": "**Forgot Passcode**\n### **Initial Steps**\n1- Enter the phone number.2- Enter the OTP.3- When the app asks for the passcode, select **\"Forgot\"**.\nAfter completing the initial steps, the user will follow one of the scenarios below:\n#### **No NID**\n- The user will be asked to create a new passcode directly after entering the SMS OTP.\n\n#### **New Device + Active Standard Card**\nThe user must enter:\n- Activation Code (8 digits)\n- National ID Number\n- The new passcode\n\n#### **New Device + Active Premium/Plus Card**\nThe user must enter:\n- Last 4 Digits of the Card\n- National ID Number\n- The new passcode\n\n#### **New Device + No Active Card**\nThe user must enter:\n- National ID Number","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","forgot","forgot passcode","login","passcode","reset passcode","الرقم السري للتطبيق","نسيت الباسكود"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Lost Mobile Access","content": "**Lost Mobile Access**\n### **Initial Steps**\n1- Press **Lost Mobile Access**.2- Enter the old phone number.3- Enter the passcode.\n### **Next Steps**\nAfter completing the initial steps, the user will follow one of the scenarios below:\n#### **No Legal Profile Yet**\n- The user will be asked to set a new phone number directly after entering the SMS OTP.\n\n#### **Not a New Device + There is a National ID**\n- The user must enter:\n- Date of Birth\n- The new Phone number\n\n#### **New Device + Active Standard Card**\nThe user must enter:\n- Activation Code\n- National ID Number\n- The new Phone number\n\n#### **New Device + Active Premium/Plus Card**\nThe user must enter:\n- Last 4 Digits of the Card\n- National ID Number\n- The new Phone number\n\n#### **New Device + No Active Card**\nThe user must enter:\n- National ID Number\n- The new Phone number","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["access","accounts","changed number","login","lost","lost phone number","mobile","غيرت الرقم","فقدت رقمي"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Login Flow","content": "**Login Flow**\n\n- Log in to the Telda app\n- ByPass Activation Code","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","flow","login"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Login","content": "**Log in to the Telda app**\n### **Login Steps:**\n1- Enter **Passcode**.2- Enter **OTP**.\n### **Login Scenarios**\n#### **Current Device**\n- After entering the Passcode and OTP, the user will be logged in successfully.\n#### **New Device + No Legal Profile**\n- After entering the Passcode and OTP, the user will be logged in successfully.\n#### **New Device + Legal Profile + No Active Card**\n- The user must enter **“Date of Birth”.**\n#### **New Device + Active Standard Card**\n- The user must enter:\n- Activation Code (8 digits)\n- National ID Number\n#### **New Device + Active Premium/Plus Card**\n- The user must enter:\n- Last 4 digits of the card\n- National ID Number","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","login"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Bypass Act","content": "**Bypass Activation Code**\nIf a user reports that they have lost their Standard, Plus or Premium Card and cannot log in to their main account because the app is asking for the Activation Code (8 digits) or the last 4 digits of the card, follow the steps below:\n1- Confirm the phone number linked to the user's main account.\n2- Complete the Full Live Check.\n3- Lock the user's Telda card.\n4- Raise a Bypass Activation Code request from the Dashboard:\n- Go to Lost Card / Device.\n- Enter the phone number linked to the account.\n- Add the chat link.\n- Verify the user's National ID number.\n- Select Bypass Activation Code.\n5- Ask the user to try logging in again.\nAfter the bypass request is processed, the app will skip the Activation Code or Last 4 Digits of the Card step and will ask the user to enter their National ID Number instead.\n**Contact Tree**\n**Request → Account Related → Bypass → Resolved**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","act","bypass","bypass activation","login","lost card login","تخطي كود التفعيل"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "OTP Related","content": "**OTP Related**\n\n**1- Transaction OTP issue:**\n**1) User did not receive OTP for online transaction**\nIf a user reports that they tried to make an online transaction but did not receive the OTP code, **ask the following:**\n1- Have you changed the mobile number linked to your Telda account within the last 24 hours?2- Have you switched your mobile network provider during this period?\n### **If the user did not change the number or network provider within 24 hours:**\nShare the following troubleshooting steps:\n- Ensure the network coverage is strong.\n- Delete unnecessary SMS messages to free phone storage.\n- Restart the phone to refresh the network.\n- Check if any apps/settings are filtering messages (e.g., Truecaller may mark Telda SMS as spam).\n**If the issue still persists after troubleshooting:**\n1- Raise **Update at MDP** request from the dashboard.**SLA: 1 BD**\n\n2- Raise Jira **\"**[Transaction OTP](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/243)**\"** and ask the user for a screenshot of the OTP page after pressing **Resend Code** to attach it to the complaint.\n**Both requests should be raised at the same time to help resolve the issue and avoid repeated contact from the user.**\n\n**If the user changed the phone number or network provider within 24 hours:**\nInform the user to wait for **24 hours**, as the new phone number/provider update needs this time to be processed. The user can try again after that period.\n\n### **2- OTP is received on the old phone number**\nIf the user confirms that the OTP is being sent to the old phone number and they **did not change the phone number within the last 24 hours**:\n1- Raise **Update at MDP** request from the dashboard.**SLA: 1 BD**\n2- Raise Jira **\"**[Transaction OTP](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/243)**\"** and ask the user for a screenshot of the OTP page to attach it to the complaint.\n\n**2- Login OTP issue:**\n- Follow the normal troubleshooting steps:\n- Ensure the network coverage is strong.\n- Delete unnecessary SMS messages to free phone storage.\n- Restart the phone to refresh the network.\n- Check if any apps/settings are filtering messages (e.g., Truecaller may mark Telda SMS as spam).\n- If the issue persists after troubleshooting, **refer the user to their network service provider.**\n\n⚠️ **Important Notes:**\n- We do **not** raise any complaints or requests for Login OTP issues, even if the user tried the troubleshooting steps.\n- Do **not** ask the user about changing their phone number or network provider for Login OTP issues.\n- Send the troubleshooting steps directly and redirect the user to the network provider if the issue continues.\n\n**3- Partners OTP issue:**\n**Impactyn / Contact / Souhoola App OTP**\nThe user will receive the OTP through the **Telda app**.\n### **If the user does not receive the OTP,** **follow these troubleshooting steps:**\n1- Make sure both applications are updated to the latest version.\n2- Make sure the user entered the phone number registered on their Telda account.\n3- Make sure the Telda app has notification permissions enabled and is running in the background.(Ensure Telda notifications are allowed from the mobile settings.)\n4- Ask the user to remove both apps and reinstall them again.\n\nIf the user is still not receiving the OTP after troubleshooting:\nRaise Jira → [BNPL Issue](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/167)","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","login","no code","otp","otp not received","related","الكود ماوصلش","رمز التحقق"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Username","content": "**Username**\nA username cannot be reused on another account, even if it was previously changed. Usernames are unique and can only be used once.\n**Username changes are allowed only once from our side, and no exceptions can be made.**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","login","username"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "App Language","content": "**App Language**\n**Android Users**\n**To change the language of the Telda app:**\n- **Tap on your Profile Picture.**\n- **Select Settings.**\n- **Tap App Language.**\n- **Choose your preferred language.**\n\n### **IOS Users**\n**To change the language of the Telda app, you will need to change the language of your iPhone from the device settings first.**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","app","language","login"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Huawei Devices","content": "**Huawei Devices**\n\n**If you receive a complaint from a Huawei user regarding:**\n- The Telda app crashed.\n- Being unable to download the Telda app.\n- Being unable to use the Telda app on their device.\n### **Process**\n- **Do not raise a Jira ticket.**\n- Inform the user that we are still working on releasing the Telda app on **Huawei AppGallery**, and it is currently unavailable.\n- Advise the user to try using another supported device.\n### **Tree**\n**Complaint → App related → App Crash  IOS or Android**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","devices","huawei","login"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Swap Number request","content": "**Swap Number request**\nA Swap Phone Number request should only be raised when:\n- The user has lost access to the registered mobile number on the main account.\n- The user does not remember the app passcode.\n**Both conditions must be confirmed before raising the swap request.**\n\n### **Required Information for Swap Request:**\n**✅ Live Check:**\n- Clear photo of the front and back sides of the National ID linked to the account.\n- Clear selfie of the ID holder while holding the front side of the National ID. (Please review the previous chats. If the user has already sent the same selfie before, please ask them to provide a new one )\n- Proof (New Mobile Number Contract)\nThis is required to complete the verification process and assist the user.\n### **✅****User Must Confirm One of These Requirements:**\n- Last 4 digits of the card number.\n- Current account balance.\n- Device type associated with the account that has the active card.\n⚠️ **Note:**If the user does not confirm any of the above requirements, raise the request anyway and the BO team will decide whether to proceed.BO will check from their side.\n- If the user has a previous swap number, review the previous chats in Freshchat to verify whether the user submitted the same live check before, and compare the photos with the ones previously submitted.\n- Call the user on the new phone number.\n- Check Truecaller and verify whether a WhatsApp account is linked to this number.\n### **How to Raise a Swap Request:**\n1- Get the user's ID using:\n- National ID number, or Phone number linked to the main account.\n2- Open the main account on the Dashboard.\n3- Click on Swap Phone Number.\n4- In the search bar, add the User ID from the account the user contacted us from and press Enter.\n5- Add the chat link, then press Swap.\n⚠️ **Important:****Do not forget to add the chat link so the Back Office team can validate the request and avoid rejection.**\n\n**SLA : 2 Working days (****suspended now** **) NO SLA**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","change phone number","login","number","request","swap","swap number","استبدال الرقم","تغيير الرقم"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "security and privacy","content": "**Live check** A live check can be used for clarifications or request submissions only within 2 hours of completion.\nIf more than 2 hours have passed, a new live check is required before providing clarification or raising a request.\n**Date of Birth**\n\nThe user's date of birth must not be disclosed.\nWe can only inform the user that the date of birth is the same as the one shown on the National ID uploaded to the account.\n**Deleted Account Recovery**\nAlways check the account deletion reason before proceeding with any recovery request.\nIf the account was deleted due to fraud, the recovery request should be rejected and must not be processed.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","and","login","privacy","security"]},{"category": "Accounts & Login","title": "Removing a Saved Visa / Card","content": "**Removing a Saved Visa / Card**\n**To remove a saved visa/card from the Telda app, ask the user to follow these steps:**\n1- Open the Telda app.2- Tap Add Money.3- The saved card will appear under the Saved Cards section.4- Swipe the card to the left to remove it.\n\n**Important:**\n- The user must activate their Telda card first **(Pick up his 1st card and activate it)**.\n- If the Telda card is not activated, the user will receive an error when tapping Add Money and will not be able to access or remove saved cards until the card is activated.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["accounts","card","login","removing","saved","visa"]},{"category": "Account Blocks & Onboarding","title": "Account Blocked","content": "**Account Blocked**\n\n- **Blocked KYC**\n- **Hard Block**\n- **Blocked Activity**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","blocked","blocks","onboarding"]},{"category": "Account Blocks & Onboarding","title": "Blocked KYC","content": "**Blocked KYC**\n\nThe owner of the uploaded NID must visit the branch to sign a new KYC.\n\nThe account will be activated within 5 working days from the date the user visits the branch.\n\nIf the account is still blocked after **5 working days** from signing the new KYC, raise the case on the **“ID Identifying Channel”** with an **SLA of 2 working days**.\n\nUser ID:\nBranch:\nVisit Date & Time:\nIssue: Blocked KYC - The user visited the branch and completed a new KYC, but the account is still blocked.\nChat Link:\n**Note**:\n- The KYC team may call some users and ask them to send the front and back of their NID if their account is blocked KYC.\n\n- So, we should first search for the user’s ID on Slack before directing them to the branch.\nhar","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","account blocked kyc","blocked","blocked kyc","blocks","kyc","onboarding","الحساب متوقف","محظور"]},{"category": "Account Blocks & Onboarding","title": "Hard Block","content": "Hard Block with no reason means that we checked the request icon on the Dashboard  and we didn't find the admin who blocked the account .. Note : We are not raising call requests for users whose accounts are '**' HARD BLOCKED ''**.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","block","blocks","hard","onboarding"]},{"category": "Account Blocks & Onboarding","title": "1 st Top Up","content": "**First top-up refund**\n### **1- Foreigners**\nA First Top-Up Refund can be raised for foreign users because foreign branches are currently unavailable, which means the user cannot receive their card.\nRefund Reason:\n- *The branch isn't available.*\n\n### **2- Egyptians**\nA First Top-Up Refund can be raised in the following cases:\n- There is no nearby branch available for the user.\n- The user is currently outside Egypt and will not return soon to pick up the card.\n\n### **Process**\n- Raise a Jira ticket under [1st Top-Up Refund](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/247).\n- SLA: 3 Business Days.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","blocks","onboarding","top"]},{"category": "Account Blocks & Onboarding","title": "1st Top Up-reactivation","content": "**1st Top-Up reactivation**\n\nIf a user asks how to reactivate their Telda account after receiving a **1st Top-Up Refund** or complains that the account is blocked:\n1- Check the **Request** section on the Dashboard.2- If the account was blocked by **Saber**, this indicates that the user previously requested a 1st Top-Up Refund, the refund was processed and the account was blocked afterward.3- Search Jira using the **User ID** to locate the related complaint.4- Send the user the screenshot of the refund transfer that was uploaded to the Jira ticket.\n\n### **Account Re-Activation**\nIf the user wants to reactivate the account, ask them to transfer the refunded amount using one of the following methods:\n- **InstaPay:** [https://ipn.eg/S/saberq20/instapay/2QJNwZ](https://ipn.eg/S/saberq20/instapay/2QJNwZ)\n- **Telda Username:** @saberq10\nThe user must provide a screenshot of the transfer.\n\n### **Process**\n- Raise a Jira ticket under [1st Top-Up Re-Activation](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/248).\n- **SLA:** 2 Business Days.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","blocks","first deposit refund","first top up refund","onboarding","reactivation","top","أول شحن","استرجاع أول إيداع"]},{"category": "Account Blocks & Onboarding","title": "Foreigners onboarding","content": "**SUSPENDED****(No foreigner branches available until further notice)Foreigners on onboarding**Foreigners are not required to make a deposit to receive the standard card.\nOnce they sign their KYC, they can make a deposit and request a Premium or Plus card. **(Premium and Plus cards cannot be ordered before completing the KYC process**)\n.We accept English and Arabic passports ONLY\nSo, if a foreigner wants to get the card and their passport is not in English or Arabic, it will not be possible to receive the card.**Required Documents**\n- Valid passport\n- Valid residency permit\n- Proof of income\nIf the applicant is a student:\n- Student ID\n- Proof of income from the parent or guardian responsible for their expensesWe can raise a reject passport within 1 working day via slack Then they can visit one of the available branches to override the new passportBranches that serve foreigners are labeled \"Foreigners\" in the locations list\n-The passport must be valid. If the passport is expired—even if it has an extension—it will be considered invalid. (See the image below for reference.)\n-This is not a passport, it is a travel document, which the user cannot use to apply for the card","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","blocks","foreigner card","foreigners","onboarding","passport","اجانب","جواز سفر"]},{"category": "Account Blocks & Onboarding","title": "Foreigners on Boarding","content": "- The foreigner will go to the branch with all the required documents.\n- They will sign the KYC.\n- They will receive the card.\n- The foreigner will not be able to activate the card unless they get the bank’s approval.\n- Bank approval will be within 2 working days.-So, if the user reaches us complaining that they cannot activate the card:we will ask them ''from which branch they received the card''? If it is ''Banque Du Caire - 6th of October''\n\n-We will inform them that they can activate the card only after getting the bank’s approval within 2 WD, and the app will auto update to allow activation.\n\n-If they are still unable to activate the card after 2 working days, we will raise it as a branch complaint.\n**This applies ONLY to Banque Du Caire - 6th of October.**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","blocks","boarding","foreigners","onboarding"]},{"category": "Account Blocks & Onboarding","title": "NID","content": "- The National ID must be valid for at least 14 days when the user goes to receive the card.\n- Reject NID<ID Identifying channel<SLA 1 WD","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","blocks","nid","onboarding"]},{"category": "Account Blocks & Onboarding","title": "Change Bank Name","content": "**Change Bank Name**\n\n### **Before Raising the Request**\n**The KYC Form State must be completed.**\n**If the KYC Form State is not completed, explain to the user that they need to wait until the KYC is reviewed and approved by the bank. This process can take up to 30 days from the date the KYC was signed at the branch.**\n**Once the KYC Form State is completed, a Change Bank Name request can be raised.**\n**SLA: 24 Hours**\n\n### **Steps**\n**1- Open the Dashboard and check the KYC Form State.**\n- **It must be completed.**\n**2- Click Change Bank Name.**\n**3- Enter the user's current full name.**\n**4- Enter the user's new full name.**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","bank","bank name","blocks","change","change name","name","onboarding","تغيير الاسم"]},{"category": "Account Blocks & Onboarding","title": "Card Pick-Up Policy","content": "**Card Pick-Up PolicyImportant Update Regarding Card Pick-Up Policy**\n\nTelda Ambassadors can now go to crowded areas outside Telda booths, such as malls, centers, or any other busy locations, to present Telda and if the person agrees to get Telda card, Telda Ambassador can proceed to give them the card.\n\n- They can transfer 50 EGP to the user so the card can be ready for pick-up then sign the KYC to get the card.\n- Users can return the 50 EGP either in cash or via a P2P transfer after activating the card.\n- This is a new card activation process so no need to raise a complaint for such cases.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","blocks","card","onboarding","pick","policy"]},{"category": "Account Blocks & Onboarding","title": "App Signing Up Flow","content": "**App Signing Up Flow:**\nIf the user is signing up and reaches out to ask whether it's possible to change their plan, we must first check the user's version:\n\n**Regarding version (1,2,3 or 4) their flow as the following:**\n1.Delivery Address (city, and area).\n2.National ID.\n3.TopUp (Card, Fawry)\n4.Subscription Plan Choice.\nSo the user can make the deposit then choose his plan\n**Regarding Version 5 as the following:**\n1.National ID.\n2.Subscription Plan Choice.\n3.Delivery Address (city, and area, and only if paid plan full street address, and  building number).\n4.TopUp (Card, Fawry, Cash at location, Request from Friend).**So there's no availability for version 5 to choose plus/premium at first then after the deposit changes the plan to standard**\n**He can choose standard at first then upgrade to premium/plus normally but not vice versa**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","app","blocks","flow","onboarding","signing"]},{"category": "Fraud","title": "Fraud Cases","content": "**Fraud Cases**\n\n- Online Transactions\n\n- POS Transactions\n\n- Account Compromised\n\n- Visa Cards","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["cases","fraud","unauthorized transaction","احتيال","معملتش المعاملة دي","نصب"]},{"category": "Fraud","title": "Fraud - Pos trx","content": "**Fraud - POS Transactions**\n\nWhen a user reports a POS transaction that they did not make, **first ask whether they have lost their Telda card.**\n#### **If the Card Was Lost**\n- Lock the card.\n- Advise the user to order a new card.\n\n#### **If the Card Is Still with the User**\n- Explain that POS transactions are made using the physical card at a merchant's POS machine.\n- A POS transaction can only be completed using the physical card, either by contactless or by inserting it into the POS machine.\n- Ask the user to check with family members, as they may have used the card and made the transaction.\n\n### **➡️Chargeback Eligibility**\n- **Chargebacks are not allowed for any POS transactions, whether they were made through Apple Pay, PIN, or contactless payments.**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["fraud","pos","trx","unauthorized transaction","احتيال","معملتش المعاملة دي","نصب"]},{"category": "Fraud","title": "Fraud - Online trx","content": "**Fraud - Online Transactions**\nWhen a user reports an online transaction that they did not make, first check whether the transaction was authenticated using **OTP (3DS)**.\n### **How to Check**\n- Open the user's account using the **User ID**.\n- Open the transaction.\n- Click **Metadata**.\n- Check whether **3DS** is present.\n\n**➡️****If the Transaction is 3DS (OTP Used)**\nThis means the transaction was authenticated using an OTP.\n- We **cannot raise a chargeback** in this case.\n- Explain to the user that the transaction required an OTP and could not have been completed without entering that code.\n- Ask the user to **lock the card** from the app.\n- Ask the user to check with family and friends who may have access to the card details.\n- The user can also contact the merchant and investigate the transaction using the **RRN**.\n- Advise the user to order a new card if they believe their card details have been compromised.\n\n**➡️****If the Transaction is NOT 3DS (No OTP Used)**\n\n### Lock the card.\n### Ask whether anyone (family or friends) knows their card details.\n### If the user has made previous transactions with the same merchant but is reporting a specific transaction they did not make, we can ask them to contact the merchant.\n### if the merchant is unknown and the user has never made a transaction with that merchant before, there is no need to refer them to the merchant.\n### Delete all linked tokens (if the transaction was made through Apple Pay).\n### Ask the user to order a new card.\n### **Please avoid putting too much pressure on the user to provide proof, as they may already be frustrated by the situation. Instead, clearly explain why the proof is important and how it helps us investigate and support the chargeback process in such cases.**\n\nChargeback Eligibility\nIf the merchant doesn’t help the user, a chargeback can be raised. (The transaction must **not be made using an OTP**)\n**Before raising a chargeback, the user must:**\n- The chargeback can only be filed when the original card is permanently blocked.\n- Wait until the transaction status becomes **Completed** in the app.\n- Provide a screenshot of the merchant’s response (if available).\n- Provide a screenshot of the transaction history from the merchant's app or website (Amazon, Talabat, Vodafone, etc.).\n\n**Important note** We can raise chargeback on the recurring transactions (subscriptions)","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["fraud","online","trx","unauthorized transaction","احتيال","معملتش المعاملة دي","نصب"]},{"category": "Fraud","title": "Account Compromised","content": "**Account Compromised**\nIf a user contacts us and reports that someone called them, asked for an OTP, and they were logged out of their account. When they tried to log in again, a new account was created.\n### **Required Actions**\n1- Complete the **full live check** with the user.2- Logout device3- Ask the required **swap questions**.4- Raise a **Swap Request**.5- **Lock the Telda card**.\n### **Urgent Escalation**\nRequest that the account be blocked as soon as possible to help protect the user's funds if they have not been used yet.\nSend the following information on the [Fraud Cases channel](https://teldaapp.slack.com/archives/C0B9RRH85AA) and mention **BO / TL / SME**:\n- **National ID Number:**\n- **Issue:** Account Compromised – Kindly lock the user's account.\n- **Chat Link:**\n**After raising the Swap Request:**\n- Inform the user not to share any OTPs, card details or personal information with anyone.\n- Advise them to **order a new card** after the Swap Request is approved.\n### **Important Note**\n- Act on these cases as quickly as possible.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","account compromised","compromised","fraud","hacked","otp scam","اتهكر","حد دخل حسابي"]},{"category": "Fraud","title": "Fraud - bank cards","content": "**Fraud - Bank Cards**\nWhen a user reports that an amount was deducted from their **bank** **card** and the transaction appears as **Telda**, but they do not recognize it.\nAsk the user for:\n- A screenshot of the SMS/message showing the deduction.\nThe following details can usually be obtained from the screenshot, but make sure to confirm them with the user:\n- Date & Time\n- Amount\n- Last 4 digits of the Visa card\n\n### **Escalation Process**\nReport the case in the **CB Channel** using the following template:\n@channel Fraud Alert\n**User ID:Phone Number:Date & Time:Amount:** EGP**Last 4 Digits of the Card:Chat Link:**\nAdd all screenshots provided by the user.\n\nAfter reporting the case, advise the user to contact their bank and raise a **fraud report**. Please note that there is **no SLA.**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["bank","cards","fraud","unauthorized transaction","احتيال","معملتش المعاملة دي","نصب"]},{"category": "Fraud","title": "Fraud -Apple pay","content": "**Apple Pay - Fraud**\n\n- **Apple Pay Fraud - POS Transactions**\n- **Apple Pay Fraud - Online Transactions**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["apple","apple pay","fraud","pay","provisioning","unauthorized transaction","wallet","ابل باي","احتيال","محفظة","معملتش المعاملة دي","نصب"]},{"category": "Fraud","title": "POS Transactions","content": "**Fraud Apple Pay POS Transaction**\nWhen a user reports an Apple Pay POS transaction that they did not make, first check the tokenization details from the dashboard.\n- Check the number of devices linked to the Apple Pay tokenization.\n- Ask the user how many devices are linked to their account.\n- If the number of linked devices does not match the user's knowledge\n- Delete the unknown device from the dashboard.\n- Raise an Apple Pay Fraud request on the transaction .\n\n**Fraud Type**\nIf the user suspects that someone from their friends or personal circle used the device/card, select Friendly Fraud.\nIf the user does not recognize the device or has no knowledge of the transaction, select Hostile .\n\n**Chargeback Eligibility**\nMake sure to clarify to the user that chargebacks are not available for Apple Pay transactions.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["fraud","pos","transactions"]},{"category": "Fraud","title": "Online Transactions","content": "**Fraud Apple Pay Online Transaction**\n\nWhen a user reports a fraudulent Apple Pay online transaction and only one device is found linked to their account.\n\n- Ask them if they linked their card with apple pay or not  If they confirmed  please ask for a screenshot from the user apple wallet\n- And clarify that there is no way to deduct an amount from apple pay without confirming the transaction\n\nImportant Note\n\nPlease be aware that if the transaction is a subscription payment and the user previously used Apple Pay for the initial payment, future recurring charges may continue to be processed as Apple Pay transactions.\n(even if it is not only one device )\nIf the user states that they do not know anything about Apple Pay and have never linked their card to it, clarify that Apple Pay can only be linked through the Apple Wallet or the app.\n\nExplain that linking a card requires either the physical card details or an OTP verification step.\n\nThe card cannot be successfully added without completing the required verification process.\n\n**Delete All token from the dashboard**\n\nRaise an Apple Pay Fraud request on the transaction .\n\n⚠️**Chargeback Eligibility**\nMake sure to clarify to the user that chargebacks are not available for Apple Pay transactions.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["fraud","online","transactions"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "Space","content": "**Space**\n**All You Need to Know About Spaces**\n### **Main Goal:**\nSpaces help users avoid spending all their money at once by allowing them to put money aside for any future goal.\nThe service is **completely free:**\n- No transfer fees.\n- No monthly fees.\n- No annual fees.\n\n### **Spaces Allows Users To:**\n✅ Choose a goal.✅ Choose a deadline for the goal.✅ Use the **Round-up feature**.\n\n### **Round-up Feature:**\nUsers do not need to manually transfer money to their Space.\nThey can select Round-up and choose the amount to round up to:\n- 5 EGP\n- 10 EGP\n- 20 EGP\n- 50 EGP\n- 100 EGP\nThe difference from each payment will automatically be transferred to their Space.\n**Important Notes:**\n- There is **no interest** on Spaces.\n- To spend money from Space, the user must first move it back to their main balance.\n\n**Disable Round-up Feature**\nTo disable Round-up:\n1- Click on the **4 squares icon**.2- Select the **Space account**.3- **Round-up** and disable the feature.\n\n**How to Delete a Space**\nTo delete a Space:\n1- Click on the **4 squares icon**.2- Select the **Space account**.3- Click on the **gear icon** at the top.4- Click **Delete Space**.\n⚠️ **Important Note:**Users cannot delete a Space while it has funds inside. They need to move the funds first, then delete the Space.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","features","other","round up","save money","space","spaces","ادخار","هدف"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "Latest app Update","content": "**Latest app UpdateOverview:**-We changed the application interface to be smoother and show the points count on the home screen as well.\n\n-The last 3 transactions will be available on the home screen. If the user wants to check all the transactions, they will click on See all\n\n-Dark mood is added to the application. Click on the profile icon, then go to display mode, and choose the mode\n\n**These changes applied to Android and iPhone as well**\n\n**Customize Background:There’s a new update available in the app that allows you to customize your background.**\n\nTo use this feature, users need to make sure they’ve updated the app to the latest version.\n\n**Once updated, they need to follow these simple steps to change the background:**\n- Open the app.\n- Tap the three dots (⋮) at the top right corner of the screen.\n- Select \"Background\" from the menu.\n- Choose your preferred background from the available options.\n- Tap \"Save\" to apply your new background.\n\n**Change transaction Category:➡️Changing the withdrawal transactions category is available only using IOS devices, and not available through android devices.**\n\n**📱****Latest app version:1.Users will see their remaining balance in the purchases push notifications Users can 2.Now pay using partial points and external cards for Vouchers and Gift Cards Users 3.Will find Vouchers and Online payments in Home Screen**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","features","latest","other","update"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "Points Mismatch","content": "**Points MismatchIf a user reports a points mismatch, we will raise the case in the Marketing channel, not on Jira.**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","features","mismatch","other","points","points expiry","النقاط","صلاحية النقاط"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "peer to peer","content": "**Peer to peer transfersPeer Profile Details:**\n- Tap into a new “Peer Profile” screen from your conversation to:\n- View total money sent and total money received between you and that peer.\n- List all transactions shared between you.\n- Block user is now available at the transaction if the user is not at the contact list, means if you have a transfer from other peer and you need to block him, you can from the old transfer (chat transfer)\n- If the user receives a transfer by mistake, they can send the amount back to the sender, as the username will be visible in the transfer details\n\n**💸****For peer to peer transfers requests, the expiry date is 10 days.**\n**This means if the user receives a request and takes no action (neither approve nor reject), the request will remain pending for 10 days.**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","features","other","peer"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "first Deposit","content": "- To make the deposit and view the available methods, the user should click on “Get Your Card Now”, not “Add Money”.\n- If the user clicks “Add Money”, they will receive a message stating that the account is not yet activated. Instead, they should click “Get Your Card”.\n- If they need the account number or RNN to make the first Fawry deposit, they can follow the below:\n- Get Your Card → Fawry → Account Number.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","deposit","features","first","other"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "App support Issue","content": "**App support Issue**\n**Update regarding users who can’t contact us through the app support**\n\nMost of the user have an emoji in their name or using a font from a non-native keyboard, so as a troubleshooting step we can\n**ask them to remove the emoji, restart the app and try again**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","features","issue","other","support"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "App Features","content": "**Sharing Transactions**\nUsers can share or send their transactions\n\n**Screenshot**\n\nAndroid users can now take screenshots directly from the app, in addition to sharing the transaction\n**Donations**Donations are now available on telda app, minimum transaction 10 EGP","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","features","other"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "Limits","content": "**Fake Limits:Fake limit issue:**\nFake limit means that the user’s account is a Full Limit account, but when making a payment, it gets declined with the reason “exceeded monthly limit.”\n**➡️What should we do?**\nFirst, check the user’s limit (to make sure it's a full access and not exceeded the limit)\ncheck transaction declined reason\nIf confirmed, raise it on Jira form as a fake limit case.\n\n**SLA: 2 WD**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","exceeded limit","fake limit","features","limits","other","الحد","تخطيت الحد"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "Refund Balance Issue","content": "**Refund Balance Issue**\n**If a user reports that a refund transaction appears on their account, but the amount is not reflected in the balance:**\nWe are currently facing an issue with updating the balance, and it has been fixed.\n### **Steps:**\n1- Search on the Dashboard using the User ID.2- Confirm the updated balance shown on the Dashboard to the user.3- Ask the user to reopen the app by closing it completely from the background/running apps.4- The balance should be updated.\n**⚠️ What NOT to say:**\n- Do not ask the user to uninstall and reinstall the app.\n**Contact Tree:**Query → Balance Inquiry → Know My Balance → Resolved.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","balance","features","issue","merchant refund","other","refund","refund not received","استرجاع فلوس","المبلغ يرجع","ريفاند"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "Points","content": "**Points Expiry Date:**The points program now has an expiry policy➡️Points are valid for 2 years from the date they’re earned.Users who had points older than 2 years and didn’t redeem them will now see those points as expired.🟢Moving forward, any points earned will automatically expire once they pass the 2-year mark.\nAlso please note :\nThere’s a term stating that the points program can be updated at any time, including changes to the expiry period.\n↪️If that happens, users will be notified with the new expiry timeframe.\n\n**For users who ask for more details:**\n↪️They can tap the question mark (?) next to “Points Balance” in the app.**This will show them all the points Terms & Conditions, including expiry info.**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","features","other","points","points expiry","النقاط","صلاحية النقاط"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "Telda Recap","content": "**Telda Recap**\n\n**Telda Recap** is available only for users who meet all the following criteria:\n- First transaction was made **before December 2025**.\n- Completed at least **10 transactions**.\n- Total spending is at least **2,000 EGP**.\n\n**Contact Tree:**Query → Telda Features → What is Telda → Resolved","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","features","other","recap","telda"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "Payroll","content": "💳If the user contacts us asking about payroll availabilityWe will ask them about the following:Full Name:His/Her Position:Company Name:Contact No.:Employees Number:**Then send this template to ‘’Sarah Ahmed’’ privately**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","features","other","payroll","salary","الراتب","مرتبات"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "Activate Investment Account","content": "**Activate Investment Account:**\n\nUsers can now activate their investment account without completing the payment KYC.\n\nHowever, to activate the Telda card, the user still needs to visit a branch to sign the KYC documents.\n\n**Important Note:**\nThere is a known issue affecting some users who have already activated their **Investment Account** and later want to activate their **Payment Account**.\n- The user visits the branch to sign the KYC and receive their card.\n- When the usher scans the National ID, the tablet does not detect the existing Investment Account due to a technical issue.\n- As a result, the usher creates a new account and completes the KYC process.\n- The user receives the card, but can’t activate it because the ID is linked to a different account.\n- The user ends up with **two accounts under the same National ID**:\n- Investment Account\n- Payment Account\n- Each account has a different User ID.\n### **Current Status**\n- The Tech Team is aware of the issue and is currently working on a fix.\n- There is **no available solution at the moment**.\n### **Action Required**\n- Raise a Jira ticket under **\"**[Card Activation](https://telda.atlassian.net/jira/software/c/projects/CS/form/204)**\"**.\n- There is currently **no SLA** for these cases.\n- Wait for further updates from the Tech Team.","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["account","activate","app","features","investment","investment account","other","استثمار","حساب استثماري"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "Contact Tree","content": "- Hard Block, close chat as Resolved\n\n- During any outage, the ticket status will be set to \"Resolved.\"\n\n[Contact Tree sheet ](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1_AtKDiM2mo4bpAoh9TFocwr_jtpxncCsRSW8zHVngQo/edit?gid=0#gid=0)","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","contact","features","other","tree"]},{"category": "App Features & Other","title": "Mubasher","content": "**Mubasher** **(Du Trade)** **withdrawal not reflected**The user states that they transferred funds from Mubasher to their Telda account, but the money has not appeared in their balance yet. Ask the user to provide a screenshot/proof of the transaction from the Mubasher app, similar to the example below.\nsend the following email**Email Template:**\n- **To:** Settlement Team\n- **CC:** Customer Support\n- **Subject:** Mubasher Withdrawal Not ReflectedUser ID: Full name in Arabic Phone number registered with Du Trade:   Transaction type: (collection) Transaction Date: Amount: **SLA: 3WD** **Mubasher Deposit not reflected** We need to ask the user for a proof document, similar to the example below from Mubasher app\n**Email Template:**\n- **To:** Settlement Team\n- **CC:** Customer Support\n- **Subject:** Mubasher Deposit Not Reflected - [Insert User ID]\nUser ID: Full name in Arabic Phone number registered with Du Trade:   Transaction type: (Deposit) Transaction Date: Amount: **SLA :3WD**","notionUrl": "https://app.notion.com/p/38e5d4fc3408812a9c68ddf28a0b67c6","keywords": ["app","du trade","features","mubasher","other","مباشر"]}];
